---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.CompleteExternalIdentitiesProjectsLocationsRequest
---@field parent string Required. The parent location resource name, such as `projects/*/locations/global`.
---@field maxSuggestions? number Optional. The maximum number of user and group results to return. The service may return fewer than this value. If unspecified, at most 6 results will be returned. The limit is distributed as evenly as possible across users and groups. For example, if max_suggestions is 7, the service may return 4 users and 3 groups. If there are fewer suggestions of one type than half the limit, the other type may return more suggestions up to the max_suggestions limit.
---@field useScimIdentities? boolean Optional. Whether to use scim identities for external identity completion. If false, we will call the Microsoft graph API to fetch the external identities.
---@field entityTypeFilter? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.CompleteExternalIdentitiesProjectsLocationsEntityTypeFilterEnum|string Optional. The type of entities to fetch. If not set, all entity types will be returned.
---@field prefixQuery? string Required. The prefix to search for. The matching is case-insensitive. * Users: * Supported: `primary_email` (SCIM `emails[type=work]` only), `given_name`, and `family_name` by leading prefix, and `display_name` per word. * Not supported: `subject`, `external_id`, and SCIM `userName` (not stored; only used to derive `subject` when `google.subject` maps `user.userName`). * Groups: * Supported: `display_name` per word.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.CompleteQueryProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresCompletionConfigRequest
---@field suggestionTypeSpecs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAdvancedCompleteQueryRequestSuggestionTypeSpecList Optional. Specification of each suggestion type.
---@field query? string Required. The typeahead input used to fetch suggestions. Maximum length is 128 characters. The query can not be empty for most of the suggestion types. If it is empty, an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is returned. The exception is when the suggestion_types contains only the type `RECENT_SEARCH`, the query can be an empty string. The is called "zero prefix" feature, which returns user's recently searched queries given the empty query.
---@field suggestionTypes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAdvancedCompleteQueryRequestSuggestionTypesItemEnumList Optional. Suggestion types to return. If empty or unspecified, query suggestions are returned. Only one suggestion type is supported at the moment.
---@field userInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaUserInfo Optional. Information about the end user. This should be the same identifier information as UserEvent.user_info and SearchRequest.user_info.
---@field experimentIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. Experiment ids for this request.
---@field userPseudoId? string Optional. A unique identifier for tracking visitors. For example, this could be implemented with an HTTP cookie, which should be able to uniquely identify a visitor on a single device. This unique identifier should not change if the visitor logs in or out of the website. This field should NOT have a fixed value such as `unknown_visitor`. This should be the same identifier as UserEvent.user_pseudo_id and SearchRequest.user_pseudo_id. The field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128
---@field includeTailSuggestions? boolean Indicates if tail suggestions should be returned if there are no suggestions that match the full query. Even if set to true, if there are suggestions that match the full query, those are returned and no tail suggestions are returned.
---@field queryModel? string Specifies the autocomplete query model, which only applies to the QUERY SuggestionType. This overrides any model specified in the Configuration > Autocomplete section of the Cloud console. Currently supported values: * `document` - Using suggestions generated from user-imported documents. * `search-history` - Using suggestions generated from the past history of SearchService.Search API calls. Do not use it when there is no traffic for Search API. * `user-event` - Using suggestions generated from user-imported search events. * `document-completable` - Using suggestions taken directly from user-imported document fields marked as completable. Default values: * `document` is the default model for regular dataStores. * `search-history` is the default model for site search dataStores.
---@field boostSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAdvancedCompleteQueryRequestBoostSpec Optional. Specification to boost suggestions matching the condition.
---@field completionConfig string Required. The completion_config of the parent dataStore or engine resource name for which the completion is performed, such as `projects/*/locations/global/collections/default_collection/dataStores/*/completionConfig` `projects/*/locations/global/collections/default_collection/engines/*/completionConfig`.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.CompleteQueryProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresRequest
