---@field fileId? string Required. The file ID.
---@field mimeType? string Required. The media type (MIME type) of the file.

---Customer-defined policy for the assistant.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicy
---@field dataProtectionPolicy? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataProtectionPolicy Optional. Data protection policy to be used for sanitizing file uploads.
---@field bannedPhrases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseList Optional. List of banned phrases.
---@field modelArmorConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfig Optional. Model Armor configuration to be used for sanitizing user prompts and assistant responses.

---Definition of a customer-defined banned phrase. A banned phrase is not allowed to appear in the user query or the LLM response, or else the answer will be refused.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhrase
---@field phrase? string Required. The raw string content to be banned.
---@field ignoreDiacritics? boolean Optional. If true, diacritical marks (e.g., accents, umlauts) are ignored when matching banned phrases. For example, "cafe" would match "café".
---@field matchType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseMatchTypeEnum|string Optional. Match type for the banned phrase.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhrase[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyBannedPhraseMatchTypeEnum "BANNED_PHRASE_MATCH_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SIMPLE_STRING_MATCH"|"WORD_BOUNDARY_STRING_MATCH"

---Configuration for customer defined Model Armor templates to be used for sanitizing user prompts and assistant responses.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfig
---@field userPromptTemplate? string Optional. The resource name of the Model Armor template for sanitizing user prompts. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{template_id}` If not specified, no sanitization will be applied to the user prompt.
---@field responseTemplate? string Optional. The resource name of the Model Armor template for sanitizing assistant responses. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/templates/{template_id}` If not specified, no sanitization will be applied to the assistant response.
---@field failureMode? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfigFailureModeEnum|string Optional. Defines the failure mode for Model Armor sanitization.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicyModelArmorConfigFailureModeEnum "FAILURE_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FAIL_OPEN"|"FAIL_CLOSED"

---Configuration for the generation of the assistant response.
