---Discovery Engine Authorization resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorization
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the authorization. It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field serverSideOauth2? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorizationServerSideOAuth2 Server-side OAuth2 configuration.
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name of the authorization. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/authorizations/{authorization}` It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---Describes the authorizations required.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorizationConfig
---@field toolAuthorizations? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. List of required authorizations for agent to access other resources. Auth tokens will be passed to the agent as part of the request body.
---@field agentAuthorization? string Optional. The authorization that is required to invoke the agent. Auth tokens will be passed to the agent as part of the request auth header.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorizationList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorization[]

---OAuth2 configuration.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorizationServerSideOAuth2
---@field privateNetworkConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorizationServerSideOAuth2PrivateNetworkConfig Optional. Set only when the OAuth provider publishes no public endpoint, in which case a token exchange has to be routed over the private network the instance is on instead of over public egress. Leaving it unset keeps the exchange on public egress.
---@field authorizationUri? string Required. The URI the user is directed to when they need to authorize. Should include everything required for a successful authorization: OAuth ID, extra flags, etc. Example: `https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth?client_id=OAUTH_ID&scope=https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events&response_type=code&access_type=offline&prompt=consent` The `redirect_uri` parameter will be overwritten by the Vertex AI Search frontend.
---@field basicAuthenticationEnabled? boolean Optional. Whether the OAuth token exchange uses HTTP Basic authentication (`client_secret_basic`) instead of sending the client credentials in the request body (`client_secret_post`). When `true`, the credentials (`client_id:client_secret`) are Base64 encoded and sent in the `Authorization` header. Some OAuth providers (e.g. Splunk) require `client_secret_basic`. When `false` or unset, the default `client_secret_post` is used.
---@field tokenUri? string Required. The HTTP endpoint that exchanges a client authorization for an access token.
---@field pkceVerificationEnabled? boolean Optional. Whether to enable PKCE verification. https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7636#section-3.1/
---@field clientSecret? string Required. The OAuth2 client secret. Encrypted at rest.
---@field scopes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The scopes to request. Example: `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events` If omitted, no additional scopes are requested beyond those required by the authorization uri. If set, it will overwrite the scopes in the authorization uri when acquiring user authorization.
---@field clientId? string Required. The OAuth2 client ID.

---Identifies the instance hosting an OAuth provider that is reachable only over a private network.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorizationServerSideOAuth2PrivateNetworkConfig
---@field instanceResource? string Required. Resource name of the instance hosting the OAuth provider. For Looker, the Looker instance, in the form `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/instances/{instance}`.

---The configuration for the BAP connector.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBAPConfig
---@field supportedConnectorModes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBAPConfigSupportedConnectorModesItemEnumList Required. The supported connector modes for the associated BAP connection.
---@field toolspecOverride? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBAPConfigToolspecOverride Optional. Custom toolspec overrides for this connection. For Enterprise BAP connectors that support admin-curated tool definitions, this holds the (simplified) per-tool overrides. On Get, populated by the server by merging persisted overrides with live runtime tool definitions and trimming the result for UI consumption. On Update, the supplied value replaces the persisted overrides after server-side validation and merging: the `base_version` field MUST match the server's current base toolspec version (otherwise the request is rejected with a user-facing error directing the admin to re-download the latest tools first).
---@field enabledActions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The actions enabled on the associated BAP connection.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBAPConfigSupportedConnectorModesItemEnum "CONNECTOR_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DATA_INGESTION"|"ACTIONS"|"END_USER_AUTHENTICATION"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBAPConfigSupportedConnectorModesItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBAPConfigSupportedConnectorModesItemEnum|string)[]

---Customer-facing view of the admin-curated toolspec for a BAP connection. Holds the (simplified) per-tool definitions surfaced to and editable by the admin in the Discovery Engine UI. Mirrors the shape of the backend `google.cloud.connectorexecution.v1.ToolspecOverride` message, but is intentionally kept as a separate public type so the Discovery Engine API surface can evolve independently of the fed-API surface (AIP-215). Handlers convert between the two via helpers in //cloud/ml/discoveryengine/external_service/v1main/data_connector_service/lib:bap_custom_tool_util.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBAPConfigToolspecOverride
---@field baseVersion? string Required. Base toolspec version against which `tools` were authored. On Update, MUST match the server's current stable toolspec version for the connection; mismatch is rejected with a user-facing error directing the admin to re-download the latest tools first.
---@field tools? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.DocumentMapList Required. Tool definitions (one Struct per tool) that the admin has customised on top of the base toolspec returned by the fed API. REQUIRED because it is the only user-editable field in the modify API; the request must carry at least one tool.

---Response message for DocumentService.BatchGetDocumentsMetadata method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponse
---@field documentsMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataList The metadata of the Documents.

---The metadata of a Document.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadata
---@field matcherValue? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataMatcherValue The value of the matcher that was used to match the Document.
---@field dataIngestionSource? string The data ingestion source of the Document. Allowed values are: * `batch`: Data ingested via Batch API, e.g., ImportDocuments. * `streaming` Data ingested via Streaming API, e.g., FHIR streaming.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataStateEnum The state of the document.
---@field lastRefreshedTime? string The timestamp of the last time the Document was last indexed.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadata[]

---The value of the matcher that was used to match the Document.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataMatcherValue
---@field uri? string If match by URI, the URI of the Document.
---@field fhirResource? string Format: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset}/fhirStores/{fhir_store}/fhir/{resource_type}/{fhir_resource_id}

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchGetDocumentsMetadataResponseDocumentMetadataStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INDEXED"|"NOT_IN_TARGET_SITE"|"NOT_IN_INDEX"

---Response message for UserStoreService.BatchUpdateUserAvailabilities method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchUpdateUserAvailabilitiesResponse
---@field userAvailabilities? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaUserAvailabilityList The updated UserAvailabilitys.

---The inline source for the input config for BatchUpdateUserLicenses method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchUpdateUserLicensesRequestInlineSource
---@field userLicenses? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaUserLicenseList Required. A list of user licenses to update. Each user license must have a valid UserLicense.user_principal.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. The list of fields to update.

---Request message for SiteSearchEngineService.BatchVerifyTargetSites method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchVerifyTargetSitesRequest

---The BigQuery output destination configuration.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigQueryDestination
---@field tableId? string Required. The table_id of exported BigQuery table.
---@field datasetId? string Required. The ID of a BigQuery Dataset.

---BigQuery source import data from.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigQuerySource
---@field datasetId? string Required. The BigQuery data set to copy the data from with a length limit of 1,024 characters.
---@field gcsStagingDir? string Intermediate Cloud Storage directory used for the import with a length limit of 2,000 characters. Can be specified if one wants to have the BigQuery export to a specific Cloud Storage directory.
---@field partitionDate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleTypeDate BigQuery time partitioned table's _PARTITIONDATE in YYYY-MM-DD format.
---@field tableId? string Required. The BigQuery table to copy the data from with a length limit of 1,024 characters.
---@field dataSchema? string The schema to use when parsing the data from the source. Supported values for user event imports: * `user_event` (default): One UserEvent per row. Supported values for document imports: * `document` (default): One Document format per row. Each document must have a valid Document.id and one of Document.json_data or Document.struct_data. * `custom`: One custom data per row in arbitrary format that conforms to the defined Schema of the data store. This can only be used by the GENERIC Data Store vertical.
---@field projectId? string The project ID or the project number that contains the BigQuery source. Has a length limit of 128 characters. If not specified, inherits the project ID from the parent request.

---The Bigtable Options object that contains information to support the import.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptions
---@field keyFieldName? string The field name used for saving row key value in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`.
---@field families? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyMap The mapping from family names to an object that contains column families level information for the given column family. If a family is not present in this map it will be ignored.

---The column of the Bigtable.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumn
---@field encoding? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnEncodingEnum|string The encoding mode of the values when the type is not `STRING`. Acceptable encoding values are: * `TEXT`: indicates values are alphanumeric text strings. * `BINARY`: indicates values are encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` family of functions. This can be overridden for a specific column by listing that column in `columns` and specifying an encoding for it.
---@field fieldName? string The field name to use for this column in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`. If not set, it is parsed from the qualifier bytes with best effort. However, due to different naming patterns, field name collisions could happen, where parsing behavior is undefined.
---@field qualifier? string Required. Qualifier of the column. If it cannot be decoded with utf-8, use a base-64 encoded string instead.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnTypeEnum|string The type of values in this column family. The values are expected to be encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` function when the encoding value is set to `BINARY`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnEncodingEnum "ENCODING_UNSPECIFIED"|"TEXT"|"BINARY"

---The column family of the Bigtable.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamily
---@field fieldName? string The field name to use for this column family in the document. The name has to match the pattern `a-zA-Z0-9*`. If not set, it is parsed from the family name with best effort. However, due to different naming patterns, field name collisions could happen, where parsing behavior is undefined.
---@field columns? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnList The list of objects that contains column level information for each column. If a column is not present in this list it will be ignored.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyTypeEnum|string The type of values in this column family. The values are expected to be encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` function when the encoding value is set to `BINARY`.
---@field encoding? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyEncodingEnum|string The encoding mode of the values when the type is not STRING. Acceptable encoding values are: * `TEXT`: indicates values are alphanumeric text strings. * `BINARY`: indicates values are encoded using `HBase Bytes.toBytes` family of functions. This can be overridden for a specific column by listing that column in `columns` and specifying an encoding for it.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyEncodingEnum "ENCODING_UNSPECIFIED"|"TEXT"|"BINARY"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamily }

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnFamilyTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRING"|"NUMBER"|"INTEGER"|"VAR_INTEGER"|"BIG_NUMERIC"|"BOOLEAN"|"JSON"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumn[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptionsBigtableColumnTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STRING"|"NUMBER"|"INTEGER"|"VAR_INTEGER"|"BIG_NUMERIC"|"BOOLEAN"|"JSON"

---The Cloud Bigtable source for importing data.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableSource
---@field bigtableOptions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBigtableOptions Required. Bigtable options that contains information needed when parsing data into typed structures. For example, column type annotations.
---@field instanceId? string Required. The instance ID of the Cloud Bigtable that needs to be imported.
---@field projectId? string The project ID that contains the Bigtable source. Has a length limit of 128 characters. If not specified, inherits the project ID from the parent request.
