---Response for EngineService.CheckFeaturePolicyMembers method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckFeaturePolicyMembersResponse
---@field memberChecks? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckFeaturePolicyMembersResponseMemberCheckList One result per requested member, in request order. Members are checked independently, so two emails for the same Google group both pass.
---@field directorySource? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckFeaturePolicyMembersResponseDirectorySourceEnum Where the project's groups are looked up.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckFeaturePolicyMembersResponseDirectorySourceEnum "DIRECTORY_SOURCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"GOOGLE"|"SCIM"|"NONE"

---The result for one requested member.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckFeaturePolicyMembersResponseMemberCheck
---@field member? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineFeaturePolicyMember The member as EngineService.UpdateEngine would save it: `id` normalized, `display_name` taken from the directory when it has one, and `verification` set. Echoes the request's member when `status` is an INVALID_ARGUMENT from the member's format.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleRpcStatus OK when the member is valid and, for a group, in the directory. Otherwise INVALID_ARGUMENT for a malformed member or a group the directory doesn't have, and UNAVAILABLE for a Google group the directory couldn't be asked about. EngineService.UpdateEngine fails on all of these, except that it leaves out an allowed group the directory doesn't have, saves the other members, and lists the group in Engine.feature_policy_rejections.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckFeaturePolicyMembersResponseMemberCheckList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckFeaturePolicyMembersResponseMemberCheck[]

---Response message for the GroundedGenerationService.CheckGrounding method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponse
---@field citedChunks? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFactChunkList List of facts cited across all claims in the answer candidate. These are derived from the facts supplied in the request.
---@field citedFacts? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunkList List of facts cited across all claims in the answer candidate. These are derived from the facts supplied in the request.
---@field claims? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponseClaimList Claim texts and citation info across all claims in the answer candidate.
---@field supportScore? number The support score for the input answer candidate. Higher the score, higher is the fraction of claims that are supported by the provided facts. This is always set when a response is returned.

---Fact chunk for grounding check.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunk
---@field chunkText? string Text content of the fact chunk. Can be at most 10K characters long.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunkList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponseCheckGroundingFactChunk[]

---Text and citation info for a claim in the answer candidate.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponseClaim
---@field groundingCheckRequired? boolean Indicates that this claim required grounding check. When the system decided this claim doesn't require attribution/grounding check, this field will be set to false. In that case, no grounding check was done for the claim and therefore citation_indices should not be returned.
---@field citationIndices? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.IntegerList A list of indices (into 'cited_chunks') specifying the citations associated with the claim. For instance [1,3,4] means that cited_chunks[1], cited_chunks[3], cited_chunks[4] are the facts cited supporting for the claim. A citation to a fact indicates that the claim is supported by the fact.
---@field endPos? number Position indicating the end of the claim in the answer candidate, exclusive, in bytes. Note that this is not measured in characters and, therefore, must be rendered as such. For example, if the claim text contains non-ASCII characters, the start and end positions vary when measured in characters (programming-language-dependent) and when measured in bytes (programming-language-independent).
---@field claimText? string Text for the claim in the answer candidate. Always provided regardless of whether citations or anti-citations are found.
---@field score? number Confidence score for the claim in the answer candidate, in the range of [0, 1]. This is set only when `CheckGroundingRequest.grounding_spec.enable_claim_level_score` is true.
---@field startPos? number Position indicating the start of the claim in the answer candidate, measured in bytes. Note that this is not measured in characters and, therefore, must be rendered in the user interface keeping in mind that some characters may take more than one byte. For example, if the claim text contains non-ASCII characters, the start and end positions vary when measured in characters (programming-language-dependent) and when measured in bytes (programming-language-independent).

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponseClaimList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingResponseClaim[]

---Specification for the grounding check.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckGroundingSpec
---@field citationThreshold? number The threshold (in [0,1]) used for determining whether a fact must be cited for a claim in the answer candidate. Choosing a higher threshold will lead to fewer but very strong citations, while choosing a lower threshold may lead to more but somewhat weaker citations. If unset, the threshold will default to 0.6.
---@field enableClaimLevelScore? boolean The control flag that enables claim-level grounding score in the response.

---Response message for the DataConnectorService.CheckRefreshToken method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckRefreshTokenResponse
---@field refreshTokenInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaRefreshTokenInfo Info about the stored refresh token.

---Response for the CheckRequirement method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckRequirementResponse
---@field metricResults? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckRequirementResponseMetricQueryResultList Metric results.
---@field requirementCondition? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleTypeExpr The condition for evaluating the requirement result.
---@field requirement? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaRequirement Requirement definition.
---@field oldestMetricTimestamp? string Timestamp of the oldest calculated metric (i.e. the most stale metric). Indicates that the `result` may not accurately reflect any Event and Product Catalog updates performed after this time.
---@field result? string The result of the requirement. It should be one of the `severity` fields in the requirement definition. If any error happens during the evaluation, it will be `UNKNOWN`.

---Metric result. The metric are in the requirement_condition.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckRequirementResponseMetricQueryResult
---@field unit? string The unit in which this metric is reported. Follows [The Unified Code for Units of Measure](https://unitsofmeasure.org/ucum.html) standard.
---@field name? string This metric query name is mapping to variables in the requirement_condition.
---@field value? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleMonitoringV3TypedValue Value of the metric query.
---@field metricType? string Type identifier of the metric corresponding to this query result.
---@field timestamp? string Time corresponding to when this metric value was calculated.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckRequirementResponseMetricQueryResultList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCheckRequirementResponseMetricQueryResult[]

---Chunk captures all raw metadata information of items to be recommended or searched in the chunk mode.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunk
---@field id? string Unique chunk ID of the current chunk.
---@field name? string The full resource name of the chunk. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document_id}/chunks/{chunk_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field annotationMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkAnnotationMetadataList Output only. The annotation metadata includes structured content in the current chunk.
---@field relevanceScore? number Output only. Represents the relevance score based on similarity. Higher score indicates higher chunk relevance. The score is in range [-1.0, 1.0]. Only populated on SearchResponse.
---@field dataUrls? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Output only. Image Data URLs if the current chunk contains images. Data URLs are composed of four parts: a prefix (data:), a MIME type indicating the type of data, an optional base64 token if non-textual, and the data itself: data:,
---@field documentMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkDocumentMetadata Metadata of the document from the current chunk.
---@field pageSpan? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkPageSpan Page span of the chunk.
---@field derivedStructData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.DocumentMap Output only. This field is OUTPUT_ONLY. It contains derived data that are not in the original input document.
---@field content? string Content is a string from a document (parsed content).
---@field annotationContents? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Output only. Annotation contents if the current chunk contains annotations.
---@field chunkMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkChunkMetadata Output only. Metadata of the current chunk.

---The annotation metadata includes structured content in the current chunk.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkAnnotationMetadata
---@field structuredContent? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkStructuredContent Output only. The structured content information.
---@field imageId? string Output only. Image id is provided if the structured content is based on an image.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkAnnotationMetadataList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkAnnotationMetadata[]

---Metadata of the current chunk. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkChunkMetadata
---@field previousChunks? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkList The previous chunks of the current chunk. The number is controlled by SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.ChunkSpec.num_previous_chunks. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.
---@field nextChunks? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaChunkList The next chunks of the current chunk. The number is controlled by SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.ChunkSpec.num_next_chunks. This field is only populated on SearchService.Search API.

---Document metadata contains the information of the document of the current chunk.
