---@field displayName? string Required. The Collection display name. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Collection was created at.
---@field dataConnector? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataConnector Output only. The data connector, if present, manages the connection for data stores in the Collection. To set up the connector, use DataConnectorService.SetUpDataConnector method, which creates a new Collection while setting up the DataConnector singleton resource. Setting up connector on an existing Collection is not supported. This output only field contains a subset of the DataConnector fields, including `name`, `data_source`, `entities.entity_name` and `entities.data_store`. To get more details about a data connector, use the DataConnectorService.GetDataConnector method.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCollectionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCollection[]

---Response message for CompletionService.CompleteExternalIdentities.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompleteExternalIdentitiesResponse
---@field externalIdentities? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaExternalIdentityList The list of external identities that match the query.

---Response message for CompletionService.CompleteQuery method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompleteQueryResponse
---@field querySuggestions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestionList Results of the matched query suggestions. The result list is ordered and the first result is a top suggestion.
---@field tailMatchTriggered? boolean True if the returned suggestions are all tail suggestions. For tail matching to be triggered, include_tail_suggestions in the request must be true and there must be no suggestions that match the full query.

---Suggestions as search queries.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestion
---@field suggestion? string The suggestion for the query.
---@field completableFieldPaths? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList The unique document field paths that serve as the source of this suggestion if it was generated from completable fields. This field is only populated for the document-completable model.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompleteQueryResponseQuerySuggestion[]

---Config to customize Autocomplete API response for both engines and data stores. Some fields are applicable to only one of them.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompletionConfig
---@field minPrefixLength? number The minimum number of characters needed to be typed in order to get suggestions. min_prefix_length must lie within the range of [1, 20]. If not set or set to 0, it will be set to the default of 1 character.
---@field enableMode? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompletionConfigEnableModeEnum The enable mode of autocomplete generation pipelines. If this field is unset, the server behavior defaults to CompletionConfig.EnableMode.AUTOMATIC. Applies to DataStore only. Ignored for Engine.
---@field shouldServeContentSuggestions? boolean Whether to generate and serve content suggestions. This allows for content suggestions to be served in addition to query suggestions.
---@field maxSuggestions? number The maximum number of autocomplete suggestions returned per term. max_suggestions must lie within the range of [1, 20]. If not set or set to 0, it will be set to the default of 20 suggestions.
---@field queryModel? string The data model of query suggestions for serving. Currently supported values: * `automatic` - autocomplete backend automatic selects or mixes suggestions from different models. * `document` - Using suggestions generated from user-imported documents. * `search-history` - Using suggestions generated from the past history of SearchService.Search API calls. Do not use it when there is no traffic for Search API. * `user-event` - Using suggestions generated from user-imported search events. * `document-completable` - Using suggestions taken directly from user-imported document fields marked as completable. If query model is empty, the serving applies the "automatic" model by default.
---@field matchingOrder? string The matching order for autocomplete suggestions, e.g., a query consisting of `sh` with `out-of-order` specified would suggest `women's shoes`, whereas a query of `red s` with `exact-prefix` specified would suggest `red shoes`. Currently supported values: * `out-of-order` * `exact-prefix` Default value: `exact-prefix`.
---@field filterPiiSuggestionsUsingDlp? boolean Deprecated: this field has no effect. As of May 2025, PII suggestion filtering using [DLP](https://cloud.google.com/security/products/dlp) is always on for all data stores and can't be configured per data store.
---@field queryFrequencyThreshold? number This field is only meaningful for suggestions generated from user events or search history. If a query shows up less than this threshold, it may indicate that the query is rarely searched and thus will not be generated as a suggestion. This is field can be helpful for preventing PII queries becoming suggestions, as those queries are usually uniquely searched. If not set, the default value is 8 used in the generation pipeline.
---@field numUniqueUsersThreshold? number This field is only meaningful for suggestions generated from user events or search history, which may have user ids attached. If the number of unique users that have searched a query is less than this threshold, the query will not be generated as a suggestion. This is field can be helpful for preventing PII queries becoming suggestions, as those queries are usually uniquely searched. If not set, the default value is 3 used in the generation pipeline.
---@field name? string Required. Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/*/dataStores/*/completionConfig` `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/dataStores/*/completionConfig` `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/engines/*/completionConfig`

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompletionConfigEnableModeEnum "ENABLE_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AUTOMATIC"|"MANUAL"

---Detailed completion information including completion attribution token and clicked completion info.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompletionInfo
---@field selectedSuggestion? string Optional. End user selected CompleteQueryResponse.QuerySuggestion.suggestion.
---@field selectedPosition? number End user selected CompleteQueryResponse.QuerySuggestion.suggestion position, starting from 0.

---Autocomplete suggestions that are imported from Customer.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompletionSuggestion
---@field globalScore? number Global score of this suggestion. Control how this suggestion would be scored / ranked.
---@field suggestion? string Required. The suggestion text.
---@field frequency? string Frequency of this suggestion. Will be used to rank suggestions when score is not available.
---@field languageCode? string BCP-47 language code of this suggestion.
---@field groupId? string If two suggestions have the same groupId, they will not be returned together. Instead the one ranked higher will be returned. This can be used to deduplicate semantically identical suggestions.
---@field alternativePhrases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Alternative matching phrases for this suggestion.
---@field groupScore? number The score of this suggestion within its group.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompletionSuggestionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCompletionSuggestion[]

---Defines circumstances to be checked before allowing a behavior
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCondition
---@field queryTerms? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionQueryTermList Search only A list of terms to match the query on. Cannot be set when Condition.query_regex is set. Maximum of 10 query terms.
---@field activeTimeRange? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionTimeRangeList Range of time(s) specifying when condition is active. Maximum of 10 time ranges.
---@field queryRegex? string Optional. Query regex to match the whole search query. Cannot be set when Condition.query_terms is set. Only supported for Basic Site Search promotion serving controls.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCondition[]

---Matcher for search request query
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionQueryTerm
---@field fullMatch? boolean Whether the search query needs to exactly match the query term.
---@field value? string The specific query value to match against Must be lowercase, must be UTF-8. Can have at most 3 space separated terms if full_match is true. Cannot be an empty string. Maximum length of 5000 characters.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionQueryTermList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionQueryTerm[]

---Used for time-dependent conditions.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionTimeRange
---@field endTime? string End of time range. Range is inclusive. Must be in the future.
---@field startTime? string Start of time range. Range is inclusive.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionTimeRangeList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionTimeRange[]

---A data sync run of DataConnector. After DataConnector is successfully initialized, data syncs are scheduled at DataConnector.refresh_interval. A ConnectorRun represents a data sync either in the past or onging that the moment. //
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRun
---@field entityRuns? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRunList Output only. The details of the entities synced at the ConnectorRun. Each ConnectorRun consists of syncing one or more entities.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time when the connector run started.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunStateEnum Output only. The state of the sync run.
---@field trigger? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunTriggerEnum Output only. The trigger for this ConnectorRun.
---@field stateUpdateTime? string Timestamp at which the connector run sync state was last updated.
---@field name? string Output only. The full resource name of the Connector Run. Format: `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/dataConnector/connectorRuns/*`. The `connector_run_id` is system-generated.
---@field latestPauseTime? string Output only. The time when the connector run was most recently paused.
---@field errors? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleRpcStatusList Contains info about errors incurred during the sync. Only exist if running into an error state. Contains error code and error message. Use with the `state` field.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time when the connector run ended.

---Represents an entity that was synced in this ConnectorRun.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRun
---@field errors? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleRpcStatusList The errors from the entity's sync run. Only exist if running into an error state. Contains error code and error message.
---@field indexedRecordCount? string Optional. The number of documents indexed.
---@field statsUpdateTime? string The timestamp for either extracted_documents_count, indexed_documents_count and error_documents_count was last updated.
---@field progress? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRunProgress Metadata to generate the progress bar.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRunStateEnum The state of the entity's sync run.
---@field stateUpdateTime? string Timestamp at which the entity sync state was last updated.
---@field sourceApiRequestCount? string Optional. The number of requests sent to 3p API.
---@field syncType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRunSyncTypeEnum Sync type of this run.
---@field deletedRecordCount? string Optional. The number of documents deleted.
---@field entityName? string The name of the source entity.
---@field errorRecordCount? string Optional. The total number of documents failed at sync at indexing stage.
---@field scheduledRecordCount? string Optional. The number of documents scheduled to be crawled/extracted from connector source. This only applies to third party connectors.
---@field extractedRecordCount? string Optional. The number of documents extracted from connector source, ready to be ingested to VAIS.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRunList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRun[]

---Represents the progress of a sync run.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRunProgress
---@field totalCount? string The total.
---@field percentile? number Derived. The percentile of the progress.current_count / total_count. The value is between [0, 1.0] inclusive.
---@field currentCount? string The current progress.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRunStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"RUNNING"|"SUCCEEDED"|"FAILED"|"OVERRUN"|"CANCELLED"|"PENDING"|"WARNING"|"SKIPPED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunEntityRunSyncTypeEnum "SYNC_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FULL"|"INCREMENTAL"|"REALTIME"|"SCALA_SYNC"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRun[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"RUNNING"|"SUCCEEDED"|"FAILED"|"OVERRUN"|"CANCELLED"|"PENDING"|"WARNING"|"SKIPPED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConnectorRunTriggerEnum "TRIGGER_UNSPECIFIED"|"SCHEDULER"|"INITIALIZATION"|"RESUME"|"MANUAL"

---The contact info stored in resource level. If both project level and resource level is populated, the resource level contact info will override the project level contact info.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaContactDetails
---@field emailAddress? string Optional. The email address of the contact.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaContactDetailsList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaContactDetails[]

---Defines a conditioned behavior to employ during serving. Must be attached to a ServingConfig to be considered at serving time. Permitted actions dependent on `SolutionType`.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControl
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSolutionTypeEnum Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field name? string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`
---@field redirectAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field useCases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field filterAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field promoteAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.
---@field conditions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.

---Adjusts order of products in returned list.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostAction
---@field dataStore? string Required. Specifies which data store's documents can be boosted by this control. Full data store name e.g. projects/123/locations/global/collections/default_collection/dataStores/default_data_store
---@field filter? string Required. Specifies which products to apply the boost to. If no filter is provided all products will be boosted (No-op). Syntax documentation: https://cloud.google.com/retail/docs/filter-and-order Maximum length is 5000 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field fixedBoost? number Optional. Strength of the boost, which should be in [-1, 1]. Negative boost means demotion. Default is 0.0 (No-op).
---@field boost? number Strength of the boost, which should be in [-1, 1]. Negative boost means demotion. Default is 0.0 (No-op).
---@field interpolationBoostSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpec Optional. Complex specification for custom ranking based on customer defined attribute value.

---Specification for custom ranking based on customer specified attribute value. It provides more controls for customized ranking than the simple (condition, boost) combination above.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpec
---@field attributeType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecAttributeTypeEnum|string Optional. The attribute type to be used to determine the boost amount. The attribute value can be derived from the field value of the specified field_name. In the case of numerical it is straightforward i.e. attribute_value = numerical_field_value. In the case of freshness however, attribute_value = (time.now() - datetime_field_value).
---@field interpolationType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecInterpolationTypeEnum|string Optional. The interpolation type to be applied to connect the control points listed below.
---@field fieldName? string Optional. The name of the field whose value will be used to determine the boost amount.
---@field controlPoints? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPointList Optional. The control points used to define the curve. The monotonic function (defined through the interpolation_type above) passes through the control points listed here.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecAttributeTypeEnum "ATTRIBUTE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NUMERICAL"|"FRESHNESS"

---The control points used to define the curve. The curve defined through these control points can only be monotonically increasing or decreasing(constant values are acceptable).
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPoint
---@field attributeValue? string Optional. Can be one of: 1. The numerical field value. 2. The duration spec for freshness: The value must be formatted as an XSD `dayTimeDuration` value (a restricted subset of an ISO 8601 duration value). The pattern for this is: `nDnM]`.
---@field boostAmount? number Optional. The value between -1 to 1 by which to boost the score if the attribute_value evaluates to the value specified above.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPointList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecControlPoint[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostActionInterpolationBoostSpecInterpolationTypeEnum "INTERPOLATION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"LINEAR"

---Specified which products may be included in results. Uses same filter as boost.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlFilterAction
---@field dataStore? string Required. Specifies which data store's documents can be filtered by this control. Full data store name e.g. projects/123/locations/global/collections/default_collection/dataStores/default_data_store
---@field filter? string Required. A filter to apply on the matching condition results. Required Syntax documentation: https://cloud.google.com/retail/docs/filter-and-order Maximum length is 5000 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControl[]

---Promote certain links based on some trigger queries. Example: Promote shoe store link when searching for `shoe` keyword. The link can be outside of associated data store.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlPromoteAction
---@field dataStore? string Required. Data store with which this promotion is attached to.
---@field searchLinkPromotion? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchLinkPromotion Required. Promotion attached to this action.

---Redirects a shopper to the provided URI.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlRedirectAction
---@field redirectUri? string Required. The URI to which the shopper will be redirected. Required. URI must have length equal or less than 2000 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSolutionTypeEnum "SOLUTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_GENERATIVE_CHAT"|"SOLUTION_TYPE_AI_MODE"

---Creates a set of terms that will act as synonyms of one another. Example: "happy" will also be considered as "glad", "glad" will also be considered as "happy".
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSynonymsAction
---@field synonyms? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Defines a set of synonyms. Can specify up to 100 synonyms. Must specify at least 2 synonyms. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlUseCasesItemEnum "SEARCH_USE_CASE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SEARCH_USE_CASE_SEARCH"|"SEARCH_USE_CASE_BROWSE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlUseCasesItemEnumList (gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlUseCasesItemEnum|string)[]

