---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFieldConfigSearchableFieldImportanceEnum "SEARCHABLE_FIELD_IMPORTANCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"VERY_LOW_IMPORTANCE"|"LOW_IMPORTANCE"|"DEFAULT_IMPORTANCE"|"HIGH_IMPORTANCE"|"VERY_HIGH_IMPORTANCE"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFieldConfigSearchableOptionEnum "SEARCHABLE_OPTION_UNSPECIFIED"|"SEARCHABLE_ENABLED"|"SEARCHABLE_DISABLED"

---Caracteristics of other file types.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileCharacteristics
---@field characteristics? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringMap Output only. Generic map of characteristics.

---Represents a file attached to a session (context file)
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileMetadata
---@field lastAddTime? string Output only. The time the file was added to the session. Note that if a file was added, then modified externally, then added again, the add time will be updated.
---@field views? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileViewMap Output only. Alternate views of this file object. Each file view is attached to a specific role. Possible example keys: - "thumbnail" - "mobile_thumbnail" - "clip" - "summary" - "translation"
---@field uploadTime? string Output only. The time the file was uploaded (If this is a file generated by an internal process and then made available to the session, this indicates the moment it happened).
---@field mimeType? string The content type of the file, see https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml.
---@field fileOriginType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileMetadataFileOriginTypeEnum Optional. The origin of the file.
---@field byteSize? string Output only. The size of the context file in bytes.
---@field downloadUri? string Output only. The AssistantService.DownloadSessionFile URL to download the file. This URL will need the same credentials as AssistantService.ListSessionFileMetadata method and will provide the resource.
---@field originalSourceType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileMetadataOriginalSourceTypeEnum Optional. The type of the original source of the file.
---@field originalUri? string Optional. The original location of the file. It may be a local file path, or any other URI that allows accessing the file in an external system. There are two scenarios in which this url may be empty: 1. If the file was sent as inline data (e.g. pasted from the clipboard). 2. If the original location is not available. Note that there's no guarantee that the URI will be pointing to a valid or actually existing file. For example, a file might have been uploaded to the session, and then deleted from the original source.
---@field fileId? string Output only. The ID of the file.
---@field metadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringMap Optional. Represents metadata related to the file that can suit particular use cases. The prefix "google." is reserved for the key for use by Google, but other prefixes can be freely used.
---@field name? string Output only. The name of the file uploaded.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileMetadataFileOriginTypeEnum "FILE_ORIGIN_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"USER_PROVIDED"|"AI_GENERATED"|"INTERNALLY_GENERATED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileMetadataList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileMetadata[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileMetadataOriginalSourceTypeEnum "FILE_SOURCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FILE_SOURCE_INLINE"|"FILE_SOURCE_LOCAL"|"FILE_SOURCE_CLOUD_STORAGE"|"FILE_SOURCE_CLOUD_DRIVE"|"FILE_SOURCE_URL"

---Represents a specific alternate version or "view" of a file object, such as a summary, a thumbnail, a translated version, etc.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileView
---@field byteSize? string Output only. The size of the view in bytes.
---@field imageCharacteristics? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaImageCharacteristics Output only. Characteristics of an image media view.
---@field uri? string Output only. The URI to access this media view.
---@field videoCharacteristics? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaVideoCharacteristics Output only. Characteristics of a video media view.
---@field fileCharacteristics? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileCharacteristics Output only. Characteristics of other file types.
---@field viewId? string Output only. Globally Unique id for this specific view.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the view was created.
---@field mimeType? string Output only. MIME type (e.g., "image/jpeg", "image/png", "text/plain", "video/mp4")

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileViewMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFileView }

---Firestore source import data from.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFirestoreSource
---@field projectId? string The project ID that the Cloud SQL source is in with a length limit of 128 characters. If not specified, inherits the project ID from the parent request.
---@field gcsStagingDir? string Intermediate Cloud Storage directory used for the import with a length limit of 2,000 characters. Can be specified if one wants to have the Firestore export to a specific Cloud Storage directory. Ensure that the Firestore service account has the necessary Cloud Storage Admin permissions to access the specified Cloud Storage directory.
---@field collectionId? string Required. The Firestore collection (or entity) to copy the data from with a length limit of 1,500 characters.
---@field databaseId? string Required. The Firestore database to copy the data from with a length limit of 256 characters.

---Cloud Storage location for input content.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaGcsSource
---@field dataSchema? string The schema to use when parsing the data from the source. Supported values for document imports: * `document` (default): One JSON Document per line. Each document must have a valid Document.id. * `content`: Unstructured data (e.g. PDF, HTML). Each file matched by `input_uris` becomes a document, with the ID set to the first 128 bits of SHA256(URI) encoded as a hex string. * `custom`: One custom data JSON per row in arbitrary format that conforms to the defined Schema of the data store. This can only be used by the GENERIC Data Store vertical. * `csv`: A CSV file with header conforming to the defined Schema of the data store. Each entry after the header is imported as a Document. This can only be used by the GENERIC Data Store vertical. Supported values for user event imports: * `user_event` (default): One JSON UserEvent per line.
---@field inputUris? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Required. Cloud Storage URIs to input files. Each URI can be up to 2000 characters long. URIs can match the full object path (for example, `gs://bucket/directory/object.json`) or a pattern matching one or more files, such as `gs://bucket/directory/*.json`. A request can contain at most 100 files (or 100,000 files if `data_schema` is `content`). Each file can be up to 2 GB (or 100 MB if `data_schema` is `content`).

---Response message for DataConnectorService.GetConnectorSecret.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaGetConnectorSecretResponse
