---@field factText? string Text content of the fact. Can be at most 10K characters long.
---@field attributes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringMap Attributes associated with the fact. Common attributes include `source` (indicating where the fact was sourced from), `author` (indicating the author of the fact), and so on.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaGroundingFactList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaGroundingFact[]

---Defines guided search spec.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaGuidedSearchSpec
---@field enableRefinementAttributes? boolean Whether or not to enable and include refinement attributes in gudied search result.
---@field enableRelatedQuestions? boolean Whether or not to enable and include related questions in search response.
---@field maxRelatedQuestions? number Max number of related questions to be returned. The valid range is [1, 5]. If enable_related_questions is true, the default value is 3.

---Config to data store for `HEALTHCARE_FHIR` vertical.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaHealthcareFhirConfig
---@field enableStaticIndexingForBatchIngestion? boolean Whether to enable static indexing for `HEALTHCARE_FHIR` batch ingestion. If set to `true`, the batch ingestion will be processed in a static indexing mode which is slower but more capable of handling larger volume.
---@field enableConfigurableSchema? boolean Whether to enable configurable schema for `HEALTHCARE_FHIR` vertical. If set to `true`, the predefined healthcare fhir schema can be extended for more customized searching and filtering.
---@field initialFilterGroups? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. Names of the Group resources to use as a basis for the initial patient filter, in format `projects/{project_id}/locations/{location_id}/datasets/{dataset_id}/fhirStores/{fhir_store_id}/fhir/Group/{group_id}`. The filter group must be a FHIR resource name of type Group, and the filter will be constructed from the direct members of the group which are Patient resources.

---Identity Mapping Entry that maps an external identity to an internal identity.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdentityMappingEntry
---@field groupId? string Group identifier. For Google Workspace user account, group_id should be the google workspace group email. For non-google identity provider, group_id is the mapped group identifier configured during the workforcepool config.
---@field userId? string User identifier. For Google Workspace user account, user_id should be the google workspace user email. For non-google identity provider, user_id is the mapped user identifier configured during the workforcepool config.
---@field externalIdentityName? string Optional. The name of the external identity.
---@field externalIdentity? string Required. Identity outside the customer identity provider. The length limit of external identity will be of 100 characters.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdentityMappingEntryList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdentityMappingEntry[]

---Identity Mapping Store which contains Identity Mapping Entries.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdentityMappingStore
---@field kmsKeyName? string Input only. The KMS key to be used to protect this Identity Mapping Store at creation time. Must be set for requests that need to comply with CMEK Org Policy protections. If this field is set and processed successfully, the Identity Mapping Store will be protected by the KMS key, as indicated in the cmek_config field.
---@field name? string Immutable. The full resource name of the identity mapping store. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/identityMappingStores/{identity_mapping_store}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field idpConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdpConfig Output only. The identity provider configuration this is bound to translate the identity mapping entries within.
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the Identity Mapping Store.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdentityMappingStoreList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdentityMappingStore[]

---The configuration for the identity data synchronization runs.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdentityScheduleConfig
---@field refreshInterval? string Optional. The refresh interval to sync the Access Control List information for the documents ingested by this connector. If not set, the access control list will be refreshed at the default interval of 30 minutes. The identity refresh interval can be at least 30 minutes and at most 7 days.
---@field nextSyncTime? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleTypeDateTime Optional. The UTC time when the next data sync is expected to start for the Data Connector. Customers are only able to specify the hour and minute to schedule the data sync. This is utilized when the data connector has a refresh interval greater than 1 day.

