---@field weight? number Optional. Weight for scores from this field. Defaults to 1.0 if not specified.
---@field key? string Required. A field key that has been indexed for Search As You Type.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestSearchAsYouTypeSpecFieldList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestSearchAsYouTypeSpecField[]

---Session specification.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestSessionSpec
---@field queryId? string If set, the search result gets stored to the "turn" specified by this query ID. Example: Let's say the session looks like this: session { name: ".../sessions/xxx" turns { query { text: "What is foo?" query_id: ".../questions/yyy" } answer: "Foo is ..." } turns { query { text: "How about bar then?" query_id: ".../questions/zzz" } } } The user can call /search API with a request like this: session: ".../sessions/xxx" session_spec { query_id: ".../questions/zzz" } Then, the API stores the search result, associated with the last turn. The stored search result can be used by a subsequent /answer API call (with the session ID and the query ID specified). Also, it is possible to call /search and /answer in parallel with the same session ID & query ID.
---@field searchResultPersistenceCount? number The number of top search results to persist. The persisted search results can be used for the subsequent /answer api call. This field is similar to the `summary_result_count` field in SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.SummarySpec.summary_result_count. At most 10 results for documents mode, or 50 for chunks mode.

---The specification for query spell correction.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestSpellCorrectionSpec
---@field mode? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestSpellCorrectionSpecModeEnum|string The mode under which spell correction replaces the original search query. Defaults to Mode.AUTO.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestSpellCorrectionSpecModeEnum "MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUGGESTION_ONLY"|"AUTO"

---Response message for SearchService.Search method.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponse
---@field guidedSearchResult? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseGuidedSearchResult Guided search result.
---@field results? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseSearchResultList A list of matched documents. The order represents the ranking.
---@field searchLinkPromotions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchLinkPromotionList Promotions for site search.
---@field semanticState? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseSemanticStateEnum Output only. Indicates the semantic state of the search response.
---@field totalSize? number The estimated total count of matched items irrespective of pagination. The count of results returned by pagination may be less than the total_size that matches.
---@field sessionInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseSessionInfo Session information. Only set if SearchRequest.session is provided. See its description for more details.
---@field geoSearchDebugInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseGeoSearchDebugInfoList
---@field queryExpansionInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseQueryExpansionInfo Query expansion information for the returned results.
---@field redirectUri? string The URI of a customer-defined redirect page. If redirect action is triggered, no search is performed, and only redirect_uri and attribution_token are set in the response.
---@field naturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingInfo Output only. Natural language query understanding information for the returned results.
---@field nextPageToken? string A token that can be sent as SearchRequest.page_token to retrieve the next page. If this field is omitted, there are no subsequent pages.
---@field correctedQuery? string Contains the spell corrected query, if found. If the spell correction type is AUTOMATIC, then the search results are based on corrected_query. Otherwise the original query is used for search.
---@field suggestedQuery? string Corrected query with low confidence, AKA did you mean query. Compared with corrected_query, this field is set when SpellCorrector returned a response, but FPR(full page replacement) is not triggered because the corrction is of low confidence(eg, reversed because there are matches of the original query in document corpus).
---@field oneBoxResults? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseOneBoxResultList A list of One Box results. There can be multiple One Box results of different types.
---@field appliedControls? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. Controls applied as part of the Control service.
---@field summary? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseSummary A summary as part of the search results. This field is only returned if SearchRequest.ContentSearchSpec.summary_spec is set.
---@field facets? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseFacetList Results of facets requested by user.
---@field attributionToken? string A unique search token. This should be included in the UserEvent logs resulting from this search, which enables accurate attribution of search model performance. This also helps to identify a request during the customer support scenarios.

---A facet result.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseFacet
---@field dynamicFacet? boolean Whether the facet is dynamically generated.
---@field key? string The key for this facet. For example, `"colors"` or `"price"`. It matches SearchRequest.FacetSpec.FacetKey.key.
---@field values? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseFacetFacetValueList The facet values for this field.

---A facet value which contains value names and their count.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseFacetFacetValue
---@field count? string Number of items that have this facet value.
---@field interval? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaInterval Interval value for a facet, such as 10, 20) for facet "price". It matches [SearchRequest.FacetSpec.FacetKey.intervals.
---@field value? string Text value of a facet, such as "Black" for facet "colors".

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseFacetFacetValueList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseFacetFacetValue[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseFacetList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchResponseFacet[]

