---Describes general widget (or web app) UI settings as seen in the cloud console UI configuration page.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettings
---@field generativeAnswerConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsGenerativeAnswerConfig Describes generative answer configuration.
---@field enableQualityFeedback? boolean Turn on or off collecting the search result quality feedback from end users.
---@field dataStoreUiConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigDataStoreUiConfigList Per data store configuration.
---@field defaultSearchRequestOrderBy? string The default ordering for search results if specified. Used to set SearchRequest#order_by on applicable requests. https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/reference/rest/v1alpha/projects.locations.dataStores.servingConfigs/search#request-body
---@field enableSafeSearch? boolean Whether to enable safe search.
---@field enableVisualContentSummary? boolean If set to true, the widget will enable visual content summary on applicable search requests. Only used by healthcare search.
---@field interactionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsInteractionTypeEnum|string Describes widget (or web app) interaction type
---@field enableSearchAsYouType? boolean Whether to enable search-as-you-type behavior for the search widget.
---@field searchAddonSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsSearchAddonSpec Optional. SearchAddonSpec is used to disable add-ons for search. This field is only supported for search requests.
---@field resultDescriptionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsResultDescriptionTypeEnum|string Controls whether result extract is display and how (snippet or extractive answer). Default to no result if unspecified.
---@field enableAutocomplete? boolean Whether or not to enable autocomplete.
---@field disableUserEventsCollection? boolean If set to true, the widget will not collect user events.
---@field googleDrivePickerEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether the Google Drive file picker is available to end-users. Declared `optional` for the same field-presence reason as `onedrive_picker_enabled` above.
---@field modelConfigInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfo Output only. The resolved, server-side view of model selector configuration. Holds both the ordered list of models that should appear in the model selector dropdown and the model that should be selected by default. Clients should render this directly without applying their own filtering, ordering, or localization. The legacy `model_configs` map above is retained for backward compatibility with clients that have not yet migrated to consuming this field.
---@field modelConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigsValueEnumMap Output only. Maps a model name to its specific configuration for this engine. This allows admin users to turn on/off individual models. This only stores models whose states are overridden by the admin. When the state is unspecified, or model_configs is empty for this model, the system will decide if this model should be available or not based on the default configuration. For example, a preview model should be disabled by default if the admin has not chosen to enable it.
---@field enablePeopleSearch? boolean Optional. If set to true, the widget will enable people search.
---@field onedrivePickerEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether the OneDrive file picker is available to end-users. Computed by the backend from admin connector enablement (Business edition) or attached OneDrive connectors (Enterprise edition), combined with the existing `disable-onedrive-upload` admin feature. Declared `optional` so an explicitly-computed `false` is serialized with field presence. A plain proto3 `bool` drops a default `false` on the wire, which prevented clients from distinguishing "picker disabled" (`false`) from "field not populated" (unset).
---@field enableCreateAgentButton? boolean Optional. If set to true, the widget will enable the create agent button.
---@field sourceAdminDisplayNameEnabled? boolean Optional. Whether to show the admin-configured display name for data connectors in the widget sources UI (instead of the connector kind). Opt-in; defaults to false.
---@field featureToggleInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfo Output only. The resolved, server-side view of the feature toggle registry (launch stage per toggle).
---@field features? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeaturesValueEnumMap Output only. Feature config for the engine to opt in or opt out of features. Supported keys: * `agent-gallery` * `no-code-agent-builder` * `prompt-gallery` * `model-selector` * `notebook-lm` * `people-search` * `people-search-org-chart` * `bi-directional-audio` * `speech-to-text` * `feedback` * `session-sharing` * `personalization-memory` * `personalization-suggested-highlights` * `mobile-app-access` * `disable-agent-sharing` * `disable-image-generation` * `disable-video-generation` * `music-generation` * `speech-generation` * `disable-onedrive-upload` * `disable-talk-to-content` * `disable-google-drive-upload` * `disable-welcome-emails` * `disable-canvas` * `canvas-workspace` * `canvas-app-builder` * `skills` * `skill-sharing` * `skill-sharing-without-admin-approval` * `skill-security-scan` * `disable-projects` * `sobi` * `enable-end-user-sharing-with-groups` * `single-agent-orchestration` * `multi-agent-orchestration` * `cross-product-intelligence` * `workflow-agents` * `in-app-notifications` * `code-extraction` * `remote-vm` * `license-tier-badge` * `canvas-app-sharing` * `agent-marketplace` * `agent-scheduling` * `preview-agents` * `plugins`

---The resolved, server-side view of the feature toggle registry containing detailed info about each feature.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfo
---@field featureToggles? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfoFeatureToggleList Output only. The feature toggles known to the registry.

---A single feature toggle with its server-provided metadata.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfoFeatureToggle
---@field id? string Output only. Matches a key in the engine `features` map.
---@field supportsAccessPolicy? boolean Output only. Whether the engine's `feature_policies` may restrict this feature to specific users or groups. When false, EngineService.UpdateEngine rejects a policy for this feature.
---@field launchStage? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfoFeatureToggleLaunchStageEnum|string Output only. Launch stage of the feature behind a toggle.
---@field retirementDate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleTypeDate Output only. The informational date the toggle is scheduled to retire, after which the feature is on for every customer. This is for display purposes only. The system does not transition feature states automatically on this date. Only when the launch stage is set to RETIRED does the feature turn on for every customer. Unset if no retirement is scheduled.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfoFeatureToggleLaunchStageEnum "LAUNCH_STAGE_UNSPECIFIED"|"PREVIEW"|"GA"|"SCHEDULED_GA"|"DELAYED_GA"|"RETIRED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfoFeatureToggleList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeatureToggleInfoFeatureToggle[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeaturesValueEnum "FEATURE_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"FEATURE_STATE_ON"|"FEATURE_STATE_OFF"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeaturesValueEnumMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsFeaturesValueEnum|string }

---Describes configuration for generative answer.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsGenerativeAnswerConfig
---@field maxRephraseSteps? number Max rephrase steps. The max number is 5 steps. If not set or set to < 1, it will be set to 1 by default.
---@field ignoreAdversarialQuery? boolean Optional. Specifies whether to filter out queries that are adversarial.
---@field modelVersion? string The model version used to generate the answer.
---@field disableRelatedQuestions? boolean Whether generated answer contains suggested related questions.
---@field ignoreNonAnswerSeekingQuery? boolean Optional. Specifies whether to filter out queries that are not answer-seeking. The default value is `false`. No answer is returned if the search query is classified as a non-answer seeking query. If this field is set to `true`, we skip generating answers for non-answer seeking queries and return fallback messages instead.
---@field languageCode? string Language code for Summary. Use language tags defined by [BCP47](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/bcp/bcp47.txt). Note: This is an experimental feature.
---@field modelPromptPreamble? string Text at the beginning of the prompt that instructs the model that generates the answer.
---@field ignoreLowRelevantContent? boolean Optional. Specifies whether to filter out queries that are not relevant to the content.
---@field imageSource? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsGenerativeAnswerConfigImageSourceEnum|string Optional. Source of image returned in the answer.
---@field resultCount? number The number of top results to generate the answer from. Up to 10.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsGenerativeAnswerConfigImageSourceEnum "IMAGE_SOURCE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALL_AVAILABLE_SOURCES"|"CORPUS_IMAGE_ONLY"|"FIGURE_GENERATION_ONLY"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsInteractionTypeEnum "INTERACTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SEARCH_ONLY"|"SEARCH_WITH_ANSWER"|"SEARCH_WITH_FOLLOW_UPS"

---The resolved, server-side view of model selector configuration for the end-user. The backend computes this per-request by applying, in order: Mendel flag evaluation, regional availability rules based on the engine's location, and admin-panel overrides from `model_configs`. The backend is the single source of truth for this configuration; clients should render `resolved_models` directly in the model selector dropdown, in the order provided, without applying their own filtering, ordering, or localization.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfo
---@field resolvedModels? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfoResolvedModelList Output only. The list of models that are available to the end-user in the model selector, in the order in which they should be displayed.
---@field defaultModelId? string Output only. The `model_id` of the model that should be selected by default in the model selector when the end-user has not made an explicit choice. The value is always one of the `model_id`s present in `resolved_models`.
---@field autoModelId? string Output only. The `model_id` a client must send when the end-user picks the "Auto" entry (the empty `model_id`). Populated only for surfaces known to have no true "Auto" mode, where leaving the model unset would fall back to a platform default rather than a backend-chosen model. Empty on every other surface, where "Auto" is resolved server-side, and when none of the surface's ranked models is available. When set, it is always one of the non-empty `model_id`s present in `resolved_models`.

---A single model that is resolved to be available to the end-user in the model selector, with all of its localized display metadata.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfoResolvedModel
---@field family? string Output only. Groups models that render together in the selector. Models sharing a value form one group; empty means the model belongs to no group. Compared for equality only -- never parsed, and never shown to a user, so it is not localized.
---@field description? string Output only. Localized description text (e.g. `State-of-the-art reasoning`). Localized using the same locale as `display_name`.
---@field modelId? string Output only. Unique identifier of the model (e.g. `gemini-2.5-flash`, `gemini-3.1-pro-preview`). This is the same identifier that clients pass back to the assistant service to select this model. Virtual / "pseudo" models (e.g. `gemini-fast`) are also valid values here; they are resolved to the underlying concrete model on the backend.
---@field label? string Output only. Short label shown in the compact selector bar chip (e.g. `3.x Flash`) as opposed to the full `display_name` (`Gemini 3.x Flash`). Falls back to `display_name` when the backend registry does not specify a distinct short label.
---@field iconUrl? string Output only. Absolute URL of a brand mark to render instead of `icon`, for models whose vendor logo is not a GM3 glyph. `icon` stays populated as the fallback, so a client that does not render images, or that fails to fetch this one, shows the glyph instead of nothing.
---@field isPreview? boolean Output only. Whether the model is currently in preview. Clients should surface this via a "Preview" badge in the selector UI.
---@field icon? string Output only. GM3-compatible icon token associated with the model (e.g. `rocket_launch`, `bolt`, `graph_5`).
---@field adminView? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfoResolvedModelAdminView Output only. Admin-surface metadata; populated only for the Console admin Feature Control page (see `AdminView`). Unset for end-user surfaces.
---@field promoted? boolean Output only. Whether this model should be promoted in the GE chat homepage banner.
---@field displayName? string Output only. Localized display name of the model (e.g. `Gemini 3.1 Pro`). Localized server-side based on the LookupWidgetConfigRequest.language_code and LookupWidgetConfigRequest.region_code of the request.

---Admin-surface metadata. Populated only when the request originates from the Cloud Console admin "Feature Control" page; left unset for end-user surfaces (Web, Mobile). Lets the admin page render its toggle table directly from the backend instead of a hardcoded client-side registry.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfoResolvedModelAdminView
---@field enabledByDefault? boolean Output only. Whether the model is enabled when the admin has set no explicit override in `UiSettings.model_configs`. Derived from `MODEL_TAG_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT`.
---@field regions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Output only. Regions where this model is launched.
---@field adminOverridable? boolean Output only. Whether the admin can toggle this model's enabled/disabled state via `UiSettings.model_configs`. Derived from `MODEL_TAG_ADMIN_OVERRIDABLE`. When false, the model is "forced" and its state is governed by `enabled_by_default`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfoResolvedModelList gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigInfoResolvedModel[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigsValueEnum "MODEL_STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"MODEL_ENABLED"|"MODEL_DISABLED"

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigsValueEnumMap { [string]: gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsModelConfigsValueEnum|string }

---@alias gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsResultDescriptionTypeEnum "RESULT_DISPLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SNIPPET"|"EXTRACTIVE_ANSWER"

---SearchAddonSpec is used to disable add-ons for search. By default, if this field is not specified, add-ons are enabled wherever applicable.
---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettingsSearchAddonSpec
---@field kpiPersonalizationAddOnDisabled? boolean Optional. If true, disables event re-ranking and personalization to optimize KPIs & personalize results.
---@field generativeAnswerAddOnDisabled? boolean Optional. If true, generative answer add-on is disabled. Generative answer add-on includes natural language to filters and simple answers.
---@field semanticAddOnDisabled? boolean Optional. If true, semantic add-on is disabled. Semantic add-on includes embeddings and jetstream.

