---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresBranchesDocumentsRequest
---@field indexTime? string Output only. The time when the document was last indexed. If this field is populated, it means the document has been indexed. While documents typically become searchable within seconds of indexing, it can sometimes take up to a few hours. If this field is not populated, it means the document has never been indexed.
---@field content? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDocumentContent The unstructured data linked to this document. Content can only be set and must be set if this document is under a `CONTENT_REQUIRED` data store.
---@field indexStatus? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDocumentIndexStatus Output only. The index status of the document. * If document is indexed successfully, the index_time field is populated. * Otherwise, if document is not indexed due to errors, the error_samples field is populated. * Otherwise, if document's index is in progress, the pending_message field is populated.
---@field schemaId? string The identifier of the schema located in the same data store.
---@field structData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.DocumentMap The structured JSON data for the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field parentDocumentId? string The identifier of the parent document. Currently supports at most two level document hierarchy. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 63 characters.
---@field jsonData? string The JSON string representation of the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field aclInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDocumentAclInfo Access control information for the document.
---@field derivedStructData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.DocumentMap Output only. This field is OUTPUT_ONLY. It contains derived data that are not in the original input document.
---@field id? string Immutable. The identifier of the document. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field allowMissing? boolean If set to `true` and the Document is not found, a new Document is be created.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the document. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided imported 'document' to update. If not set, by default updates all fields.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresControlsRequest
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field redirectAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field useCases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field filterAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field promoteAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.
---@field conditions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Indicates which fields in the provided Control to update. The following are NOT supported: * Control.name * Control.solution_type If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresConversationsRequest
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the conversation started.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the conversation finished.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConversationStateEnum|string The state of the Conversation.
---@field messages? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConversationMessageList Conversation messages.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/dataStore/*/conversations/*` or `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/*/conversations/*`.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Conversation to update. The following are NOT supported: * Conversation.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresRequest
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the DataStore.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreIndustryVerticalEnum|string Immutable. The industry vertical that the data store registers.
---@field workspaceConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWorkspaceConfig Config to store data store type configuration for workspace data. This must be set when DataStore.content_config is set as DataStore.ContentConfig.GOOGLE_WORKSPACE.
---@field idpConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdpConfig Output only. Data store level identity provider config.
---@field advancedSiteSearchConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAdvancedSiteSearchConfig Optional. Configuration for advanced site search.
---@field documentProcessingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDocumentProcessingConfig Configuration for Document understanding and enrichment.
---@field billingEstimation? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreBillingEstimation Output only. Data size estimation for billing.
---@field isInfobotFaqDataStore? boolean Optional. If set, this DataStore is an Infobot FAQ DataStore.
---@field displayName? string Required. The data store display name. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field healthcareFhirConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaHealthcareFhirConfig Optional. Configuration for `HEALTHCARE_FHIR` vertical.
---@field kmsKeyName? string Input only. The KMS key to be used to protect this DataStore at creation time. Must be set for requests that need to comply with CMEK Org Policy protections. If this field is set and processed successfully, the DataStore will be protected by the KMS key, as indicated in the cmek_config field.
---@field iconUri? string Output only. Provides the icon URI of the data store's connector source, if this is a connector-backed data store. Empty for data stores without an associated connector source. In DataStoreService.ListDataStores and DataStoreService.GetDataStore, this is only populated when DataStoreView.DATA_STORE_VIEW_FULL is requested via ListDataStoresRequest.view or GetDataStoreRequest.view respectively.
---@field contentConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreContentConfigEnum|string Immutable. The content config of the data store. If this field is unset, the server behavior defaults to ContentConfig.NO_CONTENT.
---@field configurableBillingApproachUpdateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when configurable_billing_approach was last updated.
---@field defaultSchemaId? string Output only. The id of the default Schema associated to this data store.
---@field federatedSearchConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreFederatedSearchConfig Optional. If set, this DataStore is a federated search DataStore.
---@field solutionTypes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreSolutionTypesItemEnumList The solutions that the data store enrolls. Available solutions for each industry_vertical: * `MEDIA`: `SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION` and `SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH`. * `SITE_SEARCH`: `SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH` is automatically enrolled. Other solutions cannot be enrolled.
---@field naturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingConfig Optional. Configuration for Natural Language Query Understanding.
---@field startingSchema? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSchema The start schema to use for this DataStore when provisioning it. If unset, a default vertical specialized schema will be used. This field is only used by CreateDataStore API, and will be ignored if used in other APIs. This field will be omitted from all API responses including CreateDataStore API. To retrieve a schema of a DataStore, use SchemaService.GetSchema API instead. The provided schema will be validated against certain rules on schema. Learn more from [this doc](https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/provide-schema).
---@field servingConfigDataStore? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreServingConfigDataStore Optional. Stores serving config at DataStore level.
---@field identityMappingStore? string Immutable. The fully qualified resource name of the associated IdentityMappingStore. This field can only be set for acl_enabled DataStores with `THIRD_PARTY` or `GSUITE` IdP. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/identityMappingStores/{identity_mapping_store}`.
---@field dataProtectionPolicy? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataProtectionPolicy Optional. Specifies the data protection policy for the data store.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the DataStore was created at.
---@field aclEnabled? boolean Immutable. Whether data in the DataStore has ACL information. If set to `true`, the source data must have ACL. ACL will be ingested when data is ingested by DocumentService.ImportDocuments methods. When ACL is enabled for the DataStore, Document can't be accessed by calling DocumentService.GetDocument or DocumentService.ListDocuments. Currently ACL is only supported in `GENERIC` industry vertical with non-`PUBLIC_WEBSITE` content config.
---@field configurableBillingApproach? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreConfigurableBillingApproachEnum|string Optional. Configuration for configurable billing approach. See
---@field languageInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaLanguageInfo Language info for DataStore.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided DataStore to update. If an unsupported or unknown field is provided, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The full resource name of the data store. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresSchemasRequest
---@field jsonSchema? string The JSON representation of the schema.
---@field structSchema? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.DocumentMap The structured representation of the schema.
---@field fieldConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFieldConfigList Output only. Configurations for fields of the schema.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the schema, in the format of `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/schemas/{schema}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field allowMissing? boolean If set to true, and the Schema is not found, a new Schema is created. In this situation, `update_mask` is ignored.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresServingConfigsRequest
---@field embeddingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEmbeddingConfig Bring your own embedding config. The config is used for search semantic retrieval. The retrieval is based on the dot product of SearchRequest.EmbeddingSpec.EmbeddingVector.vector and the document embeddings that are provided by this EmbeddingConfig. If SearchRequest.EmbeddingSpec.EmbeddingVector.vector is provided, it overrides this ServingConfig.embedding_config.
---@field personalizationSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestPersonalizationSpec The specification for personalization spec. Notice that if both ServingConfig.personalization_spec and SearchRequest.personalization_spec are set, SearchRequest.personalization_spec overrides ServingConfig.personalization_spec.
---@field dissociateControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition do not associate specifications. If multiple do not associate conditions match, all matching do not associate controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. ServingConfig updated timestamp.
---@field promoteControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition promote specifications. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field onewaySynonymsControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition oneway synonyms specifications. If multiple oneway synonyms conditions match, all matching oneway synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable serving config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field diversityLevel? string How much diversity to use in recommendation model results e.g. `medium-diversity` or `high-diversity`. Currently supported values: * `no-diversity` * `low-diversity` * `medium-diversity` * `high-diversity` * `auto-diversity` If not specified, we choose default based on recommendation model type. Default value: `no-diversity`. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field createTime? string Output only. ServingConfig created timestamp.
---@field answerGenerationSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAnswerGenerationSpec Optional. The specification for answer generation.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that a serving config can be associated with.
---@field synonymsControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition synonyms specifications. If multiple synonyms conditions match, all matching synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field guidedSearchSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaGuidedSearchSpec Guided search configs.
---@field rankingExpression? string The ranking expression controls the customized ranking on retrieval documents. To leverage this, document embedding is required. The ranking expression setting in ServingConfig applies to all search requests served by the serving config. However, if `SearchRequest.ranking_expression` is specified, it overrides the ServingConfig ranking expression. The ranking expression is a single function or multiple functions that are joined by "+". * ranking_expression = function, { " + ", function }; Supported functions: * double * relevance_score * double * dotProduct(embedding_field_path) Function variables: * `relevance_score`: pre-defined keywords, used for measure relevance between query and document. * `embedding_field_path`: the document embedding field used with query embedding vector. * `dotProduct`: embedding function between embedding_field_path and query embedding vector. Example ranking expression: If document has an embedding field doc_embedding, the ranking expression could be `0.5 * relevance_score + 0.3 * dotProduct(doc_embedding)`.
---@field filterControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Filter controls to use in serving path. All triggered filter controls will be applied. Filter controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 filter controls.
---@field modelId? string The id of the model to use at serving time. Currently only RecommendationModels are supported. Can be changed but only to a compatible model (e.g. others-you-may-like CTR to others-you-may-like CVR). Required when SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field genericConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigGenericConfig The GenericConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field ignoreControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition ignore specifications. If multiple ignore conditions match, all matching ignore controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field redirectControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList IDs of the redirect controls. Only the first triggered redirect action is applied, even if multiple apply. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field customFineTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCustomFineTuningSpec Custom fine tuning configs. If SearchRequest.custom_fine_tuning_spec is set, it has higher priority than the configs set here.
---@field mediaConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigMediaConfig The MediaConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field boostControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Boost controls to use in serving path. All triggered boost controls will be applied. Boost controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 boost controls.
---@field replacementControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition replacement specifications. Applied according to the order in the list. A previously replaced term can not be re-replaced. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided ServingConfig to update. The following are NOT supported: * ServingConfig.name If not set, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/engines/{engine_id}/servingConfigs/{serving_config_id}`

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresSessionsRequest
---@field turns? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSessionTurnList Turns.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the session. This field is used to identify the session in the UI. By default, the display name is the first turn query text in the session.
---@field isPinned? boolean Optional. Whether the session is pinned, pinned session will be displayed on the top of the session list.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The labels for the session. Can be set as filter in ListSessionsRequest.
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the session started.
---@field pendingAsyncAssistOperationId? string Output only. Full resource name of an in-progress AsyncAssist operation for this session, e.g. `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/engines/*/sessions/*/operations/*`. Set when the operation starts and cleared when it finishes.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSessionStateEnum|string The state of the session.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the session finished.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/sessions/*`
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Session to update. The following are NOT supported: * Session.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresSiteSearchEngineTargetSitesRequest
---@field exactMatch? boolean Immutable. If set to false, a uri_pattern is generated to include all pages whose address contains the provided_uri_pattern. If set to true, an uri_pattern is generated to try to be an exact match of the provided_uri_pattern or just the specific page if the provided_uri_pattern is a specific one. provided_uri_pattern is always normalized to generate the URI pattern to be used by the search engine.
---@field generatedUriPattern? string Output only. This is system-generated based on the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field rootDomainUri? string Output only. Root domain of the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field failureReason? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaTargetSiteFailureReason Output only. Failure reason.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaTargetSiteTypeEnum|string The type of the target site, e.g., whether the site is to be included or excluded.
---@field siteVerificationInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSiteVerificationInfo Output only. Site ownership and validity verification status.
---@field providedUriPattern? string Required. Input only. The user provided URI pattern from which the `generated_uri_pattern` is generated.
---@field indexingStatus? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaTargetSiteIndexingStatusEnum|string Output only. Indexing status.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The target site's last updated time.
---@field name string Output only. The fully qualified resource name of the target site. `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/siteSearchEngine/targetSites/{target_site}` The `target_site_id` is system-generated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsDataStoresWidgetConfigsRequest
---@field fieldsUiComponentsMap? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUIComponentFieldMap The key is the UI component. Mock. Currently supported `title`, `thumbnail`, `url`, `custom1`, `custom2`, `custom3`. The value is the name of the field along with its device visibility. The 3 custom fields are optional and can be added or removed. `title`, `thumbnail`, `url` are required UI components that cannot be removed.
---@field collectionComponents? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigCollectionComponentList Output only. Collection components that lists all collections and child data stores associated with the widget config, those data sources can be used for filtering in widget service APIs, users can return results that from selected data sources. For SaaS / Business engines, when `LookupWidgetConfig` is called with `view = WITH_AVAILABLE_CONNECTORS`, this list is additionally augmented with synthetic placeholder entries for connectors the caller may attach but has not yet attached (see `CollectionComponent` for the placeholder contract). The frontend can therefore render a unified list of already-attached and available-to-attach sources by iterating this single field. For Enterprise engines and for the default `view`, only already-attached connectors are returned (today's behavior).
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was updated.
---@field enableSearchAsYouType? boolean Whether to enable search-as-you-type behavior for the search widget
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was created.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that this WidgetConfig can be used for.
---@field dataStoreUiConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigDataStoreUiConfigList Configurable UI configurations per data store.
---@field assistantSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigAssistantSettings Optional. Output only. Describes the assistant settings of the widget.
---@field configId? string Output only. Unique obfuscated identifier of a WidgetConfig.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable widget config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field customerProvidedConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigCustomerProvidedConfig Optional. Output only. Describes the customer related configurations, currently only used for government customers. This field cannot be modified after project onboarding.
---@field allowlistedDomains? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Allowlisted domains that can load this widget.
---@field dataStoreType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigDataStoreTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of the parent data store.
---@field enableResultScore? boolean Whether to show the result score.
---@field enableConversationalSearch? boolean Whether to allow conversational search (LLM, multi-turn) or not (non-LLM, single-turn).
---@field uiBranding? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiBrandingSettings Describes search widget UI branding settings, such as the widget title, logo, favicons, and colors.
---@field nodes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigNodeList Output only. The nodes associated with the Widget Config.
---@field accessSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigAccessSettings Will be used for all widget access settings seen in cloud console integration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field defaultSearchRequestOrderBy? string The default ordering for search results if specified. Used to set SearchRequest#order_by on applicable requests. https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/reference/rest/v1alpha/projects.locations.dataStores.servingConfigs/search#request-body
---@field allowPublicAccess? boolean Whether allow no-auth integration with widget. If set true, public access to search or other solutions from widget is allowed without authenication token provided by customer hosted backend server.
---@field enableSnippetResultSummary? boolean Turn on or off summary for each snippets result.
---@field enablePrivateKnowledgeGraph? boolean Optional. Output only. Whether to enable private knowledge graph.
---@field enableAutocomplete? boolean Whether or not to enable autocomplete.
---@field geminiBundle? boolean Output only. Whether the subscription is gemini bundle or not.
---@field enableSafeSearch? boolean Whether to enable safe search.
---@field uiSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettings Describes general widget search settings as seen in cloud console widget configuration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field facetField? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigFacetFieldList The configuration and appearance of facets in the end user view.
---@field enableWebApp? boolean Whether to enable standalone web app.
---@field enableQualityFeedback? boolean Turn on or off collecting the search result quality feedback from end users.
---@field batchAuthStatuses? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigBatchAuthStatusList Output only. The batch authorization statuses for the widget's connectors.
---@field minimumDataTermAccepted? boolean Output only. Whether the customer accepted data use terms.
---@field homepageSetting? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigHomepageSetting Optional. Describes the homepage settings of the widget.
---@field resultDisplayType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigResultDisplayTypeEnum|string The type of snippet to display in UCS widget. - RESULT_DISPLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED for existing users. - SNIPPET for new non-enterprise search users. - EXTRACTIVE_ANSWER for new enterprise search users.
---@field llmEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether LLM is enabled in the corresponding data store.
---@field contentSearchSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestContentSearchSpec The content search spec that configs the desired behavior of content search.
---@field enableSummarization? boolean Turn on or off summarization for the search response.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigIndustryVerticalEnum|string Output only. The industry vertical that the WidgetConfig registers. The WidgetConfig industry vertical is based on the associated Engine.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the widget config. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}/widgetConfigs/{widget_config_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided WidgetConfig to update. The following are the only supported fields: * WidgetConfig.enable_autocomplete If not set, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesAssistantsAgentsRequest
---@field customPlaceholderText? string Optional. The custom placeholder text that appears in the text box before the user enters any text.
---@field sharingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAgentSharingConfig Optional. The sharing config of the agent.
---@field icon? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAgentImage Optional. The icon that represents the agent on the UI.
---@field description? string Required. Human-readable description of the agent. This might be used by an LLM to automatically select an agent to respond to a user query.
---@field dialogflowAgentDefinition? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDialogflowAgentDefinition Optional. The behavior of the agent is defined as a Dialogflow agent.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAgentStateEnum|string Output only. The lifecycle state of the agent.
---@field displayName? string Required. Display name of the agent. This might be used by an LLM to automatically select an agent to respond to a user query.
---@field adkAgentDefinition? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAdkAgentDefinition Optional. The behavior of the agent is defined as an ADK agent.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability config for the agent.
---@field a2aAgentDefinition? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaA2AAgentDefinition Optional. The behavior of the agent is defined as an A2A agent.
---@field defaultPinned? boolean Optional. Whether the agent is pinned by default for users who have access to it and have not explicitly unpinned it. Setting this field requires an admin.
---@field deploymentFailureReason? string Output only. The reason why the agent deployment failed. Only set if the state is DEPLOYMENT_FAILED.
---@field creationFailureReason? string Output only. The reason why the agent creation (provisioning) failed. Only set if the state is CREATION_FAILED.
---@field rejectionReason? string Output only. The reason why the agent was rejected. Only set if the state is PRIVATE, and got there via rejection.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Agent was created.
---@field starterPrompts? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAgentStarterPromptList Optional. The starter prompt suggestions to show the user on the landing page of the agent.
---@field suspensionReason? string Output only. The reason why the agent was suspended. Only set if the state is SUSPENDED.
---@field managedAgentDefinition? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaManagedAgentDefinition Optional. The behavior of the Google managed agent.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp when this Agent was most recently updated.
---@field languageCode? string Optional. The code of the language of the text in the description, display_name and starter_prompts fields.
---@field authorizationConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAuthorizationConfig Optional. The authorizations that are required by the agent.
---@field name string Identifier. Resource name of the agent. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/assistants/{assistant}/agents/{agent}`
---@field updateMask? string Optional. The list of fields to update.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesAssistantsCannedQueriesRequest
---@field googleDefined? boolean Output only. Whether this is a Google-defined, read-only canned query.
---@field defaultTexts? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCannedQueryCannedQueryTexts Required. The default (non-localized) values for the text attributes.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the canned query. It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field requiredCapabilities? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCannedQueryAssistantCapabilityList Optional. The capabilities the Assistant needs to have to use this canned query.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether this canned query is enabled.
---@field localizedTexts? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCannedQueryCannedQueryTextsMap Optional. The translations of the text attributes. The keys should be BCP-47 language codes.
---@field updateMask? string The list of fields to update.
---@field name string Immutable. Resource name of the canned query. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/assistants/{assistant}/cannedQueries/{canned_query}` It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesAssistantsRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. The assistant display name. It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field enabledTools? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantToolListMap Optional. The enabled tools on this assistant. The keys are data connector resource names, in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataConnector`. The values are the tools that the admin enabled on that connector. Admins can selectively enable tools on any of the connectors that they created in the project. For example: ``` { "projects/my-project/locations/global/collections/jira1/dataConnector": { "toolInfo": [ { "toolName": "create_jira_issue", "toolDisplayName": "Create Jira issue" }, { "toolName": "update_jira_issue", "toolDisplayName": "Update Jira issue" } ] } } ```
---@field createTime? string Output only. Represents the time when this Assistant was created.
---@field knowledgeCatalogEnabled? boolean Optional. Indicates whether Knowledge Catalog is enabled for this specific assistant. When enabled, it powers discovery context using organizational data. If unspecified, defaults to true.
---@field disableLocationContext? boolean Optional. Indicates whether to disable user location context. By default, user location context is enabled.
---@field webGroundingType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantWebGroundingTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of web grounding to use.
---@field description? string Optional. Description for additional information. Expected to be shown on the configuration UI, not to the users of the assistant.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Represents the time when this Assistant was most recently updated.
---@field customerPolicy? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantCustomerPolicy Optional. Customer policy for the assistant.
---@field defaultWebGroundingToggleOff? boolean Optional. This field controls the default web grounding toggle for end users if `web_grounding_type` is set to `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH` or `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_ENTERPRISE_WEB_SEARCH`. By default, this field is set to false. If `web_grounding_type` is `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_GOOGLE_SEARCH` or `WEB_GROUNDING_TYPE_ENTERPRISE_WEB_SEARCH`, end users will have web grounding enabled by default on UI. If true, grounding toggle will be disabled by default on UI. End users can still enable web grounding in the UI if web grounding is enabled.
---@field generationConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAssistantGenerationConfig Optional. Configuration for the generation of the assistant response.
---@field updateMask? string The list of fields to update.
---@field name string Immutable. Resource name of the assistant. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/assistants/{assistant}` It must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesControlsRequest
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field redirectAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field useCases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field filterAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field promoteAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.
---@field conditions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Indicates which fields in the provided Control to update. The following are NOT supported: * Control.name * Control.solution_type If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesConversationsRequest
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the conversation started.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the conversation finished.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConversationStateEnum|string The state of the Conversation.
---@field messages? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConversationMessageList Conversation messages.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Conversation to update. The following are NOT supported: * Conversation.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/dataStore/*/conversations/*` or `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/*/conversations/*`.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesRequest
---@field associatedAgentRegistry? string Output only. The Agent registry containing the agents, MCP servers and tools associated with this engine. Derived server-side from the linked Agent Gateway's registry.
---@field effectiveFeatures? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineEffectiveFeaturesValueEnumMap Output only. The complete, server-resolved state of every known feature toggle. Unlike `features`, which stores only explicit admin overrides, this map always contains an entry for every toggle. Clients should read toggle state from this field.
---@field disableAnalytics? boolean Optional. Whether to disable analytics for searches performed on this engine.
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the Engine.
---@field appType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineAppTypeEnum|string Optional. Immutable. This the application type which this engine resource represents. NOTE: this is a new concept independ of existing industry vertical or solution type.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineIndustryVerticalEnum|string Optional. The industry vertical that the engine registers. The restriction of the Engine industry vertical is based on DataStore: Vertical on Engine has to match vertical of the DataStore linked to the engine.
---@field similarDocumentsConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineSimilarDocumentsEngineConfig Additional config specs for a `similar-items` engine.
---@field chatEngineConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineChatEngineConfig Configurations for the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field connectorTenantInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringMap Optional. Maps a connector ID (e.g., "hybrid-github", "shopify") to tenant-specific information required for that connector. The structure of the tenant information string is connector-dependent.
---@field featurePolicies? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineFeaturePolicyMap Optional. Per-feature access policies, keyed by feature toggle name (see `features`). A feature with no entry is available to every user when it is on. Only features that support access policies are accepted.
---@field observabilityConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaObservabilityConfig Optional. Observability config for the engine.
---@field features? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineFeaturesValueEnumMap Optional. Feature config for the engine to opt in or opt out of features. Supported keys: * `*`: all features, if it's present, all other feature state settings are ignored. * `agent-gallery` * `no-code-agent-builder` * `prompt-gallery` * `model-selector` * `notebook-lm` * `people-search` * `people-search-org-chart` * `bi-directional-audio` * `speech-to-text` * `feedback` * `session-sharing` * `personalization-memory` * `personalization-suggested-highlights` * `mobile-app-access` * `disable-agent-sharing` * `disable-image-generation` * `disable-video-generation` * `music-generation` * `speech-generation` * `disable-onedrive-upload` * `disable-talk-to-content` * `disable-google-drive-upload` * `disable-welcome-emails` * `disable-canvas` * `canvas-workspace` * `canvas-app-builder` * `skills` * `skill-sharing` * `skill-sharing-without-admin-approval` * `skill-security-scan` * `disable-projects` * `sobi` * `enable-end-user-sharing-with-groups` * `single-agent-orchestration` * `multi-agent-orchestration` * `cross-product-intelligence` * `workflow-agents` * `in-app-notifications` * `code-extraction` * `remote-vm` * `license-tier-badge` * `canvas-app-sharing` * `agent-marketplace` * `agent-scheduling` * `preview-agents` * `plugins`
---@field delayedGlobalFeatureToggleStateAllowed? boolean Output only. Whether the project is allowed to set `global_feature_toggle_state` to `DELAYED`.
---@field knowledgeGraphConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineKnowledgeGraphConfig Optional. Configurations for the Knowledge Graph. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field configurableBillingApproach? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineConfigurableBillingApproachEnum|string Optional. Configuration for configurable billing approach.
---@field dataStoreIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The data stores associated with this engine. For SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH and SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION type of engines, they can only associate with at most one data store. If solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT, multiple DataStores in the same Collection can be associated here. Note that when used in CreateEngineRequest, one DataStore id must be provided as the system will use it for necessary initializations.
---@field procurementContactEmails? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The emails of the procurement contacts.
---@field searchEngineConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineSearchEngineConfig Configurations for the Search Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field modelConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineModelConfigsValueEnumMap Optional. Maps a model name to its specific configuration for this engine. This allows admin users to turn on/off individual models. This only stores models whose states are overridden by the admin. When the state is unspecified, or model_configs is empty for this model, the system will decide if this model should be available or not based on the default configuration. For example, a preview model should be disabled by default if the admin has not chosen to enable it.
---@field globalFeatureToggleState? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineGlobalFeatureToggleStateEnum|string Optional. Controls the global feature toggle state for the engine.
---@field recommendationMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineRecommendationMetadata Output only. Additional information of a recommendation engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field chatEngineMetadata? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineChatEngineMetadata Output only. Additional information of the Chat Engine. Only applicable if solution_type is SOLUTION_TYPE_CHAT.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was created at.
---@field agentGatewaySetting? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAgentGatewaySetting Optional. The agent gateway setting for the engine.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. The solutions of the engine.
---@field mediaRecommendationEngineConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineMediaRecommendationEngineConfig Configurations for the Media Engine. Only applicable on the data stores with solution_type SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION and IndustryVertical.MEDIA vertical.
---@field commonConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineCommonConfig Common config spec that specifies the metadata of the engine.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Recommendation Engine was last updated.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the engine. Should be human readable. UTF-8 encoded string with limit of 1024 characters.
---@field marketplaceAgentVisibility? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEngineMarketplaceAgentVisibilityEnum|string Optional. The visibility of marketplace agents in the agent gallery.
---@field sessionConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSessionConfig Optional. Non-empty default. Session config for the engine.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The fully qualified resource name of the engine. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}` engine should be 1-63 characters, and valid characters are /a-z0-9*/. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Engine to update. If an unsupported or unknown field is provided, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesServingConfigsRequest
---@field embeddingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEmbeddingConfig Bring your own embedding config. The config is used for search semantic retrieval. The retrieval is based on the dot product of SearchRequest.EmbeddingSpec.EmbeddingVector.vector and the document embeddings that are provided by this EmbeddingConfig. If SearchRequest.EmbeddingSpec.EmbeddingVector.vector is provided, it overrides this ServingConfig.embedding_config.
---@field personalizationSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestPersonalizationSpec The specification for personalization spec. Notice that if both ServingConfig.personalization_spec and SearchRequest.personalization_spec are set, SearchRequest.personalization_spec overrides ServingConfig.personalization_spec.
---@field dissociateControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition do not associate specifications. If multiple do not associate conditions match, all matching do not associate controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. ServingConfig updated timestamp.
---@field promoteControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition promote specifications. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field onewaySynonymsControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition oneway synonyms specifications. If multiple oneway synonyms conditions match, all matching oneway synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable serving config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field diversityLevel? string How much diversity to use in recommendation model results e.g. `medium-diversity` or `high-diversity`. Currently supported values: * `no-diversity` * `low-diversity` * `medium-diversity` * `high-diversity` * `auto-diversity` If not specified, we choose default based on recommendation model type. Default value: `no-diversity`. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field createTime? string Output only. ServingConfig created timestamp.
---@field answerGenerationSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAnswerGenerationSpec Optional. The specification for answer generation.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that a serving config can be associated with.
---@field synonymsControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition synonyms specifications. If multiple synonyms conditions match, all matching synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field guidedSearchSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaGuidedSearchSpec Guided search configs.
---@field rankingExpression? string The ranking expression controls the customized ranking on retrieval documents. To leverage this, document embedding is required. The ranking expression setting in ServingConfig applies to all search requests served by the serving config. However, if `SearchRequest.ranking_expression` is specified, it overrides the ServingConfig ranking expression. The ranking expression is a single function or multiple functions that are joined by "+". * ranking_expression = function, { " + ", function }; Supported functions: * double * relevance_score * double * dotProduct(embedding_field_path) Function variables: * `relevance_score`: pre-defined keywords, used for measure relevance between query and document. * `embedding_field_path`: the document embedding field used with query embedding vector. * `dotProduct`: embedding function between embedding_field_path and query embedding vector. Example ranking expression: If document has an embedding field doc_embedding, the ranking expression could be `0.5 * relevance_score + 0.3 * dotProduct(doc_embedding)`.
---@field filterControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Filter controls to use in serving path. All triggered filter controls will be applied. Filter controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 filter controls.
---@field modelId? string The id of the model to use at serving time. Currently only RecommendationModels are supported. Can be changed but only to a compatible model (e.g. others-you-may-like CTR to others-you-may-like CVR). Required when SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field genericConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigGenericConfig The GenericConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field ignoreControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition ignore specifications. If multiple ignore conditions match, all matching ignore controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field redirectControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList IDs of the redirect controls. Only the first triggered redirect action is applied, even if multiple apply. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field customFineTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCustomFineTuningSpec Custom fine tuning configs. If SearchRequest.custom_fine_tuning_spec is set, it has higher priority than the configs set here.
---@field mediaConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigMediaConfig The MediaConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field boostControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Boost controls to use in serving path. All triggered boost controls will be applied. Boost controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 boost controls.
---@field replacementControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition replacement specifications. Applied according to the order in the list. A previously replaced term can not be re-replaced. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided ServingConfig to update. The following are NOT supported: * ServingConfig.name If not set, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/engines/{engine_id}/servingConfigs/{serving_config_id}`

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesSessionsRequest
---@field turns? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSessionTurnList Turns.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the session. This field is used to identify the session in the UI. By default, the display name is the first turn query text in the session.
---@field isPinned? boolean Optional. Whether the session is pinned, pinned session will be displayed on the top of the session list.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The labels for the session. Can be set as filter in ListSessionsRequest.
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the session started.
---@field pendingAsyncAssistOperationId? string Output only. Full resource name of an in-progress AsyncAssist operation for this session, e.g. `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/engines/*/sessions/*/operations/*`. Set when the operation starts and cleared when it finishes.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSessionStateEnum|string The state of the session.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the session finished.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/sessions/*`
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Session to update. The following are NOT supported: * Session.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsEnginesWidgetConfigsRequest
---@field fieldsUiComponentsMap? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUIComponentFieldMap The key is the UI component. Mock. Currently supported `title`, `thumbnail`, `url`, `custom1`, `custom2`, `custom3`. The value is the name of the field along with its device visibility. The 3 custom fields are optional and can be added or removed. `title`, `thumbnail`, `url` are required UI components that cannot be removed.
---@field collectionComponents? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigCollectionComponentList Output only. Collection components that lists all collections and child data stores associated with the widget config, those data sources can be used for filtering in widget service APIs, users can return results that from selected data sources. For SaaS / Business engines, when `LookupWidgetConfig` is called with `view = WITH_AVAILABLE_CONNECTORS`, this list is additionally augmented with synthetic placeholder entries for connectors the caller may attach but has not yet attached (see `CollectionComponent` for the placeholder contract). The frontend can therefore render a unified list of already-attached and available-to-attach sources by iterating this single field. For Enterprise engines and for the default `view`, only already-attached connectors are returned (today's behavior).
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was updated.
---@field enableSearchAsYouType? boolean Whether to enable search-as-you-type behavior for the search widget
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was created.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that this WidgetConfig can be used for.
---@field dataStoreUiConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigDataStoreUiConfigList Configurable UI configurations per data store.
---@field assistantSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigAssistantSettings Optional. Output only. Describes the assistant settings of the widget.
---@field configId? string Output only. Unique obfuscated identifier of a WidgetConfig.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable widget config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field customerProvidedConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigCustomerProvidedConfig Optional. Output only. Describes the customer related configurations, currently only used for government customers. This field cannot be modified after project onboarding.
---@field allowlistedDomains? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Allowlisted domains that can load this widget.
---@field dataStoreType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigDataStoreTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of the parent data store.
---@field enableResultScore? boolean Whether to show the result score.
---@field enableConversationalSearch? boolean Whether to allow conversational search (LLM, multi-turn) or not (non-LLM, single-turn).
---@field uiBranding? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiBrandingSettings Describes search widget UI branding settings, such as the widget title, logo, favicons, and colors.
---@field nodes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigNodeList Output only. The nodes associated with the Widget Config.
---@field accessSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigAccessSettings Will be used for all widget access settings seen in cloud console integration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field defaultSearchRequestOrderBy? string The default ordering for search results if specified. Used to set SearchRequest#order_by on applicable requests. https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/reference/rest/v1alpha/projects.locations.dataStores.servingConfigs/search#request-body
---@field allowPublicAccess? boolean Whether allow no-auth integration with widget. If set true, public access to search or other solutions from widget is allowed without authenication token provided by customer hosted backend server.
---@field enableSnippetResultSummary? boolean Turn on or off summary for each snippets result.
---@field enablePrivateKnowledgeGraph? boolean Optional. Output only. Whether to enable private knowledge graph.
---@field enableAutocomplete? boolean Whether or not to enable autocomplete.
---@field geminiBundle? boolean Output only. Whether the subscription is gemini bundle or not.
---@field enableSafeSearch? boolean Whether to enable safe search.
---@field uiSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettings Describes general widget search settings as seen in cloud console widget configuration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field facetField? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigFacetFieldList The configuration and appearance of facets in the end user view.
---@field enableWebApp? boolean Whether to enable standalone web app.
---@field enableQualityFeedback? boolean Turn on or off collecting the search result quality feedback from end users.
---@field batchAuthStatuses? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigBatchAuthStatusList Output only. The batch authorization statuses for the widget's connectors.
---@field minimumDataTermAccepted? boolean Output only. Whether the customer accepted data use terms.
---@field homepageSetting? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigHomepageSetting Optional. Describes the homepage settings of the widget.
---@field resultDisplayType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigResultDisplayTypeEnum|string The type of snippet to display in UCS widget. - RESULT_DISPLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED for existing users. - SNIPPET for new non-enterprise search users. - EXTRACTIVE_ANSWER for new enterprise search users.
---@field llmEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether LLM is enabled in the corresponding data store.
---@field contentSearchSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestContentSearchSpec The content search spec that configs the desired behavior of content search.
---@field enableSummarization? boolean Turn on or off summarization for the search response.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigIndustryVerticalEnum|string Output only. The industry vertical that the WidgetConfig registers. The WidgetConfig industry vertical is based on the associated Engine.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the widget config. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}/widgetConfigs/{widget_config_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided WidgetConfig to update. The following are the only supported fields: * WidgetConfig.enable_autocomplete If not set, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsCollectionsRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. The Collection display name. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the Collection was created at.
---@field dataConnector? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataConnector Output only. The data connector, if present, manages the connection for data stores in the Collection. To set up the connector, use DataConnectorService.SetUpDataConnector method, which creates a new Collection while setting up the DataConnector singleton resource. Setting up connector on an existing Collection is not supported. This output only field contains a subset of the DataConnector fields, including `name`, `data_source`, `entities.entity_name` and `entities.data_store`. To get more details about a data connector, use the DataConnectorService.GetDataConnector method.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the Collection. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. The list of fields to be updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresBranchesDocumentsRequest
---@field indexTime? string Output only. The time when the document was last indexed. If this field is populated, it means the document has been indexed. While documents typically become searchable within seconds of indexing, it can sometimes take up to a few hours. If this field is not populated, it means the document has never been indexed.
---@field content? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDocumentContent The unstructured data linked to this document. Content can only be set and must be set if this document is under a `CONTENT_REQUIRED` data store.
---@field indexStatus? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDocumentIndexStatus Output only. The index status of the document. * If document is indexed successfully, the index_time field is populated. * Otherwise, if document is not indexed due to errors, the error_samples field is populated. * Otherwise, if document's index is in progress, the pending_message field is populated.
---@field schemaId? string The identifier of the schema located in the same data store.
---@field structData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.DocumentMap The structured JSON data for the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field parentDocumentId? string The identifier of the parent document. Currently supports at most two level document hierarchy. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 63 characters.
---@field jsonData? string The JSON string representation of the document. It should conform to the registered Schema or an `INVALID_ARGUMENT` error is thrown.
---@field aclInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDocumentAclInfo Access control information for the document.
---@field derivedStructData? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.DocumentMap Output only. This field is OUTPUT_ONLY. It contains derived data that are not in the original input document.
---@field id? string Immutable. The identifier of the document. Id should conform to [RFC-1034](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc1034) standard with a length limit of 128 characters.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided imported 'document' to update. If not set, by default updates all fields.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the document. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/branches/{branch}/documents/{document_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field allowMissing? boolean If set to `true` and the Document is not found, a new Document is be created.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresControlsRequest
---@field synonymsAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSynonymsAction Treats a group of terms as synonyms of one another.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. What solution the control belongs to. Must be compatible with vertical of resource. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field boostAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlBoostAction Defines a boost-type control
---@field redirectAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlRedirectAction Defines a redirect-type control.
---@field useCases? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlUseCasesItemEnumList Specifies the use case for the control. Affects what condition fields can be set. Only applies to SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH. Currently only allow one use case per control. Must be set when solution_type is SolutionType.SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field filterAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlFilterAction Defines a filter-type control Currently not supported by Recommendation
---@field promoteAction? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaControlPromoteAction Promote certain links based on predefined trigger queries.
---@field conditions? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConditionList Determines when the associated action will trigger. Omit to always apply the action. Currently only a single condition may be specified. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field associatedServingConfigIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Output only. List of all ServingConfig IDs this control is attached to. May take up to 10 minutes to update after changes.
---@field displayName? string Required. Human readable name. The identifier used in UI views. Must be UTF-8 encoded string. Length limit is 128 characters. Otherwise an INVALID ARGUMENT error is thrown.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Indicates which fields in the provided Control to update. The following are NOT supported: * Control.name * Control.solution_type If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/*/locations/global/dataStore/*/controls/*`

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresConversationsRequest
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the conversation started.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the conversation finished.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConversationStateEnum|string The state of the Conversation.
---@field messages? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaConversationMessageList Conversation messages.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/dataStore/*/conversations/*` or `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/*/conversations/*`.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Conversation to update. The following are NOT supported: * Conversation.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresRequest
---@field cmekConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCmekConfig Output only. CMEK-related information for the DataStore.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreIndustryVerticalEnum|string Immutable. The industry vertical that the data store registers.
---@field workspaceConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWorkspaceConfig Config to store data store type configuration for workspace data. This must be set when DataStore.content_config is set as DataStore.ContentConfig.GOOGLE_WORKSPACE.
---@field idpConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaIdpConfig Output only. Data store level identity provider config.
---@field advancedSiteSearchConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAdvancedSiteSearchConfig Optional. Configuration for advanced site search.
---@field documentProcessingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDocumentProcessingConfig Configuration for Document understanding and enrichment.
---@field billingEstimation? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreBillingEstimation Output only. Data size estimation for billing.
---@field isInfobotFaqDataStore? boolean Optional. If set, this DataStore is an Infobot FAQ DataStore.
---@field displayName? string Required. The data store display name. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field healthcareFhirConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaHealthcareFhirConfig Optional. Configuration for `HEALTHCARE_FHIR` vertical.
---@field kmsKeyName? string Input only. The KMS key to be used to protect this DataStore at creation time. Must be set for requests that need to comply with CMEK Org Policy protections. If this field is set and processed successfully, the DataStore will be protected by the KMS key, as indicated in the cmek_config field.
---@field iconUri? string Output only. Provides the icon URI of the data store's connector source, if this is a connector-backed data store. Empty for data stores without an associated connector source. In DataStoreService.ListDataStores and DataStoreService.GetDataStore, this is only populated when DataStoreView.DATA_STORE_VIEW_FULL is requested via ListDataStoresRequest.view or GetDataStoreRequest.view respectively.
---@field contentConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreContentConfigEnum|string Immutable. The content config of the data store. If this field is unset, the server behavior defaults to ContentConfig.NO_CONTENT.
---@field configurableBillingApproachUpdateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when configurable_billing_approach was last updated.
---@field defaultSchemaId? string Output only. The id of the default Schema associated to this data store.
---@field federatedSearchConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreFederatedSearchConfig Optional. If set, this DataStore is a federated search DataStore.
---@field solutionTypes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreSolutionTypesItemEnumList The solutions that the data store enrolls. Available solutions for each industry_vertical: * `MEDIA`: `SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION` and `SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH`. * `SITE_SEARCH`: `SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH` is automatically enrolled. Other solutions cannot be enrolled.
---@field naturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaNaturalLanguageQueryUnderstandingConfig Optional. Configuration for Natural Language Query Understanding.
---@field startingSchema? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSchema The start schema to use for this DataStore when provisioning it. If unset, a default vertical specialized schema will be used. This field is only used by CreateDataStore API, and will be ignored if used in other APIs. This field will be omitted from all API responses including CreateDataStore API. To retrieve a schema of a DataStore, use SchemaService.GetSchema API instead. The provided schema will be validated against certain rules on schema. Learn more from [this doc](https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/provide-schema).
---@field servingConfigDataStore? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreServingConfigDataStore Optional. Stores serving config at DataStore level.
---@field identityMappingStore? string Immutable. The fully qualified resource name of the associated IdentityMappingStore. This field can only be set for acl_enabled DataStores with `THIRD_PARTY` or `GSUITE` IdP. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/identityMappingStores/{identity_mapping_store}`.
---@field dataProtectionPolicy? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataProtectionPolicy Optional. Specifies the data protection policy for the data store.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the DataStore was created at.
---@field aclEnabled? boolean Immutable. Whether data in the DataStore has ACL information. If set to `true`, the source data must have ACL. ACL will be ingested when data is ingested by DocumentService.ImportDocuments methods. When ACL is enabled for the DataStore, Document can't be accessed by calling DocumentService.GetDocument or DocumentService.ListDocuments. Currently ACL is only supported in `GENERIC` industry vertical with non-`PUBLIC_WEBSITE` content config.
---@field configurableBillingApproach? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaDataStoreConfigurableBillingApproachEnum|string Optional. Configuration for configurable billing approach. See
---@field languageInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaLanguageInfo Language info for DataStore.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided DataStore to update. If an unsupported or unknown field is provided, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The full resource name of the data store. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresSchemasRequest
---@field jsonSchema? string The JSON representation of the schema.
---@field structSchema? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.DocumentMap The structured representation of the schema.
---@field fieldConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFieldConfigList Output only. Configurations for fields of the schema.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the schema, in the format of `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/schemas/{schema}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field allowMissing? boolean If set to true, and the Schema is not found, a new Schema is created. In this situation, `update_mask` is ignored.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresServingConfigsRequest
---@field embeddingConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaEmbeddingConfig Bring your own embedding config. The config is used for search semantic retrieval. The retrieval is based on the dot product of SearchRequest.EmbeddingSpec.EmbeddingVector.vector and the document embeddings that are provided by this EmbeddingConfig. If SearchRequest.EmbeddingSpec.EmbeddingVector.vector is provided, it overrides this ServingConfig.embedding_config.
---@field personalizationSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestPersonalizationSpec The specification for personalization spec. Notice that if both ServingConfig.personalization_spec and SearchRequest.personalization_spec are set, SearchRequest.personalization_spec overrides ServingConfig.personalization_spec.
---@field dissociateControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition do not associate specifications. If multiple do not associate conditions match, all matching do not associate controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. ServingConfig updated timestamp.
---@field promoteControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition promote specifications. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field onewaySynonymsControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition oneway synonyms specifications. If multiple oneway synonyms conditions match, all matching oneway synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable serving config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field diversityLevel? string How much diversity to use in recommendation model results e.g. `medium-diversity` or `high-diversity`. Currently supported values: * `no-diversity` * `low-diversity` * `medium-diversity` * `high-diversity` * `auto-diversity` If not specified, we choose default based on recommendation model type. Default value: `no-diversity`. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field createTime? string Output only. ServingConfig created timestamp.
---@field answerGenerationSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAnswerGenerationSpec Optional. The specification for answer generation.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that a serving config can be associated with.
---@field synonymsControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition synonyms specifications. If multiple synonyms conditions match, all matching synonyms controls in the list will execute. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field guidedSearchSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaGuidedSearchSpec Guided search configs.
---@field rankingExpression? string The ranking expression controls the customized ranking on retrieval documents. To leverage this, document embedding is required. The ranking expression setting in ServingConfig applies to all search requests served by the serving config. However, if `SearchRequest.ranking_expression` is specified, it overrides the ServingConfig ranking expression. The ranking expression is a single function or multiple functions that are joined by "+". * ranking_expression = function, { " + ", function }; Supported functions: * double * relevance_score * double * dotProduct(embedding_field_path) Function variables: * `relevance_score`: pre-defined keywords, used for measure relevance between query and document. * `embedding_field_path`: the document embedding field used with query embedding vector. * `dotProduct`: embedding function between embedding_field_path and query embedding vector. Example ranking expression: If document has an embedding field doc_embedding, the ranking expression could be `0.5 * relevance_score + 0.3 * dotProduct(doc_embedding)`.
---@field filterControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Filter controls to use in serving path. All triggered filter controls will be applied. Filter controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 filter controls.
---@field modelId? string The id of the model to use at serving time. Currently only RecommendationModels are supported. Can be changed but only to a compatible model (e.g. others-you-may-like CTR to others-you-may-like CVR). Required when SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_RECOMMENDATION.
---@field genericConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigGenericConfig The GenericConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field ignoreControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition ignore specifications. If multiple ignore conditions match, all matching ignore controls in the list will execute. Order does not matter. Maximum number of specifications is 100.
---@field redirectControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList IDs of the redirect controls. Only the first triggered redirect action is applied, even if multiple apply. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field customFineTuningSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaCustomFineTuningSpec Custom fine tuning configs. If SearchRequest.custom_fine_tuning_spec is set, it has higher priority than the configs set here.
---@field mediaConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaServingConfigMediaConfig The MediaConfig of the serving configuration.
---@field boostControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Boost controls to use in serving path. All triggered boost controls will be applied. Boost controls must be in the same data store as the serving config. Maximum of 20 boost controls.
---@field replacementControlIds? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Condition replacement specifications. Applied according to the order in the list. A previously replaced term can not be re-replaced. Maximum number of specifications is 100. Can only be set if SolutionType is SOLUTION_TYPE_SEARCH.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided ServingConfig to update. The following are NOT supported: * ServingConfig.name If not set, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/engines/{engine_id}/servingConfigs/{serving_config_id}`

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresSessionsRequest
---@field turns? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSessionTurnList Turns.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the session. This field is used to identify the session in the UI. By default, the display name is the first turn query text in the session.
---@field isPinned? boolean Optional. Whether the session is pinned, pinned session will be displayed on the top of the session list.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Optional. The labels for the session. Can be set as filter in ListSessionsRequest.
---@field userPseudoId? string A unique identifier for tracking users.
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the session started.
---@field pendingAsyncAssistOperationId? string Output only. Full resource name of an in-progress AsyncAssist operation for this session, e.g. `projects/*/locations/*/collections/*/engines/*/sessions/*/operations/*`. Set when the operation starts and cleared when it finishes.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSessionStateEnum|string The state of the session.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the session finished.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided Session to update. The following are NOT supported: * Session.name If not set or empty, all supported fields are updated.
---@field name string Immutable. Fully qualified name `projects/{project}/locations/global/collections/{collection}/engines/{engine}/sessions/*`

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresSiteSearchEngineTargetSitesRequest
---@field exactMatch? boolean Immutable. If set to false, a uri_pattern is generated to include all pages whose address contains the provided_uri_pattern. If set to true, an uri_pattern is generated to try to be an exact match of the provided_uri_pattern or just the specific page if the provided_uri_pattern is a specific one. provided_uri_pattern is always normalized to generate the URI pattern to be used by the search engine.
---@field generatedUriPattern? string Output only. This is system-generated based on the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field rootDomainUri? string Output only. Root domain of the provided_uri_pattern.
---@field failureReason? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaTargetSiteFailureReason Output only. Failure reason.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaTargetSiteTypeEnum|string The type of the target site, e.g., whether the site is to be included or excluded.
---@field siteVerificationInfo? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSiteVerificationInfo Output only. Site ownership and validity verification status.
---@field providedUriPattern? string Required. Input only. The user provided URI pattern from which the `generated_uri_pattern` is generated.
---@field indexingStatus? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaTargetSiteIndexingStatusEnum|string Output only. Indexing status.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The target site's last updated time.
---@field name string Output only. The fully qualified resource name of the target site. `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataStores/{data_store}/siteSearchEngine/targetSites/{target_site}` The `target_site_id` is system-generated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsDataStoresWidgetConfigsRequest
---@field fieldsUiComponentsMap? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUIComponentFieldMap The key is the UI component. Mock. Currently supported `title`, `thumbnail`, `url`, `custom1`, `custom2`, `custom3`. The value is the name of the field along with its device visibility. The 3 custom fields are optional and can be added or removed. `title`, `thumbnail`, `url` are required UI components that cannot be removed.
---@field collectionComponents? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigCollectionComponentList Output only. Collection components that lists all collections and child data stores associated with the widget config, those data sources can be used for filtering in widget service APIs, users can return results that from selected data sources. For SaaS / Business engines, when `LookupWidgetConfig` is called with `view = WITH_AVAILABLE_CONNECTORS`, this list is additionally augmented with synthetic placeholder entries for connectors the caller may attach but has not yet attached (see `CollectionComponent` for the placeholder contract). The frontend can therefore render a unified list of already-attached and available-to-attach sources by iterating this single field. For Enterprise engines and for the default `view`, only already-attached connectors are returned (today's behavior).
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was updated.
---@field enableSearchAsYouType? boolean Whether to enable search-as-you-type behavior for the search widget
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the WidgetConfig was created.
---@field solutionType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigSolutionTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. Specifies the solution type that this WidgetConfig can be used for.
---@field dataStoreUiConfigs? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigDataStoreUiConfigList Configurable UI configurations per data store.
---@field assistantSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigAssistantSettings Optional. Output only. Describes the assistant settings of the widget.
---@field configId? string Output only. Unique obfuscated identifier of a WidgetConfig.
---@field displayName? string Required. The human readable widget config display name. Used in Discovery UI. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 128 characters. Otherwise, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field customerProvidedConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigCustomerProvidedConfig Optional. Output only. Describes the customer related configurations, currently only used for government customers. This field cannot be modified after project onboarding.
---@field allowlistedDomains? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.StringList Allowlisted domains that can load this widget.
---@field dataStoreType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigDataStoreTypeEnum|string Output only. The type of the parent data store.
---@field enableResultScore? boolean Whether to show the result score.
---@field enableConversationalSearch? boolean Whether to allow conversational search (LLM, multi-turn) or not (non-LLM, single-turn).
---@field uiBranding? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiBrandingSettings Describes search widget UI branding settings, such as the widget title, logo, favicons, and colors.
---@field nodes? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigNodeList Output only. The nodes associated with the Widget Config.
---@field accessSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigAccessSettings Will be used for all widget access settings seen in cloud console integration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field defaultSearchRequestOrderBy? string The default ordering for search results if specified. Used to set SearchRequest#order_by on applicable requests. https://cloud.google.com/generative-ai-app-builder/docs/reference/rest/v1alpha/projects.locations.dataStores.servingConfigs/search#request-body
---@field allowPublicAccess? boolean Whether allow no-auth integration with widget. If set true, public access to search or other solutions from widget is allowed without authenication token provided by customer hosted backend server.
---@field enableSnippetResultSummary? boolean Turn on or off summary for each snippets result.
---@field enablePrivateKnowledgeGraph? boolean Optional. Output only. Whether to enable private knowledge graph.
---@field enableAutocomplete? boolean Whether or not to enable autocomplete.
---@field geminiBundle? boolean Output only. Whether the subscription is gemini bundle or not.
---@field enableSafeSearch? boolean Whether to enable safe search.
---@field uiSettings? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigUiSettings Describes general widget search settings as seen in cloud console widget configuration page. Replaces top deprecated top level properties.
---@field facetField? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigFacetFieldList The configuration and appearance of facets in the end user view.
---@field enableWebApp? boolean Whether to enable standalone web app.
---@field enableQualityFeedback? boolean Turn on or off collecting the search result quality feedback from end users.
---@field batchAuthStatuses? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigBatchAuthStatusList Output only. The batch authorization statuses for the widget's connectors.
---@field minimumDataTermAccepted? boolean Output only. Whether the customer accepted data use terms.
---@field homepageSetting? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigHomepageSetting Optional. Describes the homepage settings of the widget.
---@field resultDisplayType? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigResultDisplayTypeEnum|string The type of snippet to display in UCS widget. - RESULT_DISPLAY_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED for existing users. - SNIPPET for new non-enterprise search users. - EXTRACTIVE_ANSWER for new enterprise search users.
---@field llmEnabled? boolean Output only. Whether LLM is enabled in the corresponding data store.
---@field contentSearchSpec? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaSearchRequestContentSearchSpec The content search spec that configs the desired behavior of content search.
---@field enableSummarization? boolean Turn on or off summarization for the search response.
---@field industryVertical? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaWidgetConfigIndustryVerticalEnum|string Output only. The industry vertical that the WidgetConfig registers. The WidgetConfig industry vertical is based on the associated Engine.
---@field name string Immutable. The full resource name of the widget config. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection_id}/dataStores/{data_store_id}/widgetConfigs/{widget_config_id}`. This field must be a UTF-8 encoded string with a length limit of 1024 characters.
---@field updateMask? string Indicates which fields in the provided WidgetConfig to update. The following are the only supported fields: * WidgetConfig.enable_autocomplete If not set, all supported fields are updated.

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsLicenseConfigsRequest
---@field alertPolicyResourceConfig? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaAlertPolicyResourceConfig Optional. The alert policy config for this license config.
---@field autoRenew? boolean Optional. Whether the license config should be auto renewed when it reaches the end date.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaLicenseConfigStateEnum|string Output only. The state of the license config.
---@field subscriptionTier? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaLicenseConfigSubscriptionTierEnum|string Required. Subscription tier information for the license config.
---@field earlyTerminated? boolean Output only. Indication of whether the subscription is terminated earlier than the expiration date.
---@field billingAccountLicenseConfig? string Output only. The name of the BillingAccountLicenseConfig from which this LicenseConfig is assigned, if this field is set.
---@field licenseCount? string Required. Number of licenses purchased.
---@field earlyTerminationDate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleTypeDate Output only. The date when the subscription is terminated earlier than the expiration date.
---@field lastUserUpdateTime? string Optional. Timestamp of the most recent user-initiated update (seat count change or subscription term change). Unlike `update_time`, this field is only stamped when a customer explicitly updates the license (e.g. via the UI), and is not touched by system-driven writes (subscription pipeline, BALC propagation, etc.).
---@field startDate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleTypeDate Required. The start date.
---@field freeTrial? boolean Optional. Whether the license config is for free trial.
---@field subscriptionTerm? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaLicenseConfigSubscriptionTermEnum|string Required. Subscription term.
---@field geminiBundle? boolean Output only. Whether the license config is for Gemini bundle.
---@field endDate? gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.GoogleTypeDate Optional. The planed end date.
---@field updateMask? string Optional. Indicates which fields in the provided LicenseConfig to update. If an unsupported or unknown field is provided, an INVALID_ARGUMENT error is returned.
---@field name string Immutable. Identifier. The fully qualified resource name of the license config. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/licenseConfigs/{license_config}`

---@class gcp.unstable.discoveryengine_v1alpha.PatchProjectsLocationsSampleQuerySetsRequest
---@field createTime? string Output only. Timestamp the SampleQuerySet was created at.
